{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink","id":881101,"title":"Can Lunars shrink?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T10:59:20-07:00","id":881101,"title":"Can Lunars shrink?","content":"I think Ant-Man's poweres are awesome (trust me, I've seen Civil War ;P)<br /> <br /> So, is there a way, or would it be fitting for lunars to get really really tiny retaining their human aspect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:09:54-07:00","id":881105,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. It seems well within their purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:42:10-07:00","id":881126,"title":"","content":"...Now I imagine a sheep lunar shrinking in the wash. Huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:52:28-07:00","id":881144,"title":"","content":"Like every Lunar question, it depends. There are some ideas of how Lunars should be that wouldn't allow it.<br /> <br /> But I say definitely yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:53:32-07:00","id":881145,"title":"","content":"Only If they took a form that was smaller than them, like say, a bunny.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, extremely unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:18:35-07:00","id":881163,"title":"","content":"I don't think shrinking works very well in a role playing game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:19:54-07:00","id":881165,"title":"","content":"As JayTee says, shrinking by taking a small animal will more than likely be an option. AntMan style shrinking with compressed badass strength? I'd guess not. <br /> <br /> Maybe as an artifact armor Evocation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:21:13-07:00","id":881168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881163#post881163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think shrinking works very well in a role playing game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on the game. I've seen it handled just fine in a number of superhero rpgs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:18:10-07:00","id":881259,"title":"","content":"Lunars can certainly change into small <i>animals</i>, but they have never had the ability to change the size of their normal form much (technically you could do Hybrid Body Rearrangement with the Giant and Tiny mutations, but I don't think that was intentional). However, it's no farther from the traditional Lunar bailiwick than some of the new stuff we see Solars doing in 3e is from theirs, so I wouldn't rule it out. If you're wondering for a Lunar NPC, I'd say go for whatever seems appropriate to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:12:31-07:00","id":881291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881259#post881259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars can certainly change into small <i>animals</i>, but they have never had the ability to change the size of their normal form much (technically you could do Hybrid Body Rearrangement with the Giant and Tiny mutations, but I don't think that was intentional). However, it's no farther from the traditional Lunar bailiwick than some of the new stuff we see Solars doing in 3e is from theirs, so I wouldn't rule it out. If you're wondering for a Lunar NPC, I'd say go for whatever seems appropriate to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/TYKg23V5BXE?list=PLCWf7Om4nic1yQ1_fsTHlMlcOR2Gztlne&amp;t=42\" target=\"_blank\">[Abridged Guyot Scream]</a><br /> <br /> HBR could only ever do partial transformations. Size-altering mutations alter the whole body, so they're a no go. We can reasonably tell this on account of the Knacks that aren't HBR that are there for altering size, like Tyrant Mouse Dominion, thus avoiding the nightmare of adjudication for rules regarding how many of which size mutation you need to use to change a form to a given size based on what animals are in your library.<br /> <br /> Also, Ill go ahead and say it based on the declarations back when EX3 was announced: Ant-Man is probably not Lunar material. He can go on the heap of other generic shapeshifters that got tossed out to thematically lean-up the Lunars, such as Mystique. (Envision me twitching an eye whenever she or any other direct, dragged and dropped with no alteration for context and flavor superhero from other media gets mentioned).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:23:37-07:00","id":881302,"title":"","content":"I never really understood why they wanted to narrow down Lunar shapeshifting themes. Even the broadest possible interpretation of shapeshifting is still significantly narrower than &quot;human excellence&quot;. And human excellence is only one part of the Solar theme set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881163#post881163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think shrinking works very well in a role playing game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:27:37-07:00","id":881305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881302#post881302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really understood why they wanted to narrow down Lunar shapeshifting themes. Even the broadest possible interpretation of shapeshifting is still significantly narrower than &quot;human excellence&quot;. And human excellence is only one part of the Solar theme set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they were never meant to broad omni-shapeshifters. They were meant to be clearly tied to Werewolf: the Apocalypse, with a few adjacent bits of other werebeast lore. Trying to fit in Odo or The Thing From Another World is a fundamental square peg round hole problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not? </div> </div> </div>Book-keeping, disproportional stat adjustments, fridge logic questions... they're loaded with them. Growing and Shrinking powers in GURPS take up at least a half a page each to handle this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:21:54-07:00","id":881373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881291#post881291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TYKg23V5BXE?list=PLCWf7Om4nic1yQ1_fsTHlMlcOR2Gztlne&amp;t=42\" target=\"_blank\">[Abridged Guyot Scream]</a><br /> <br /> HBR could only ever do partial transformations. Size-altering mutations alter the whole body, so they're a no go. We can reasonably tell this on account of the Knacks that aren't HBR that are there for altering size, like Tyrant Mouse Dominion, thus avoiding the nightmare of adjudication for rules regarding how many of which size mutation you need to use to change a form to a given size based on what animals are in your library.</div> </div> </div> </div>I concede the point to someone with actual Lunar experience!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T18:53:29-07:00","id":881405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the broadest possible interpretation of shapeshifting is still significantly narrower than &quot;human excellence&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThe broadest possible interpretation of shapeshifting contains a lot of things that either clash terribly with one another, or are rather overpowered or difficult to represent in this medium in their own right. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881302#post881302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think the user interface, so to speak, is very well suited for it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-03-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:36:42-07:00","id":881447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881305#post881305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they were never meant to broad omni-shapeshifters. They were meant to be clearly tied to Werewolf: the Apocalypse, with a few adjacent bits of other werebeast lore. Trying to fit in Odo or The Thing From Another World is a fundamental square peg round hole problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, what Lunars were originally meant to be was bad. But don't take it from me, <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:where-it-all-went-wrong\" target=\"_blank\">take it from Holden</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881305#post881305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book-keeping, disproportional stat adjustments, fridge logic questions... they're loaded with them. Growing and Shrinking powers in GURPS take up at least a half a page each to handle this stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's GURPS. I think that I, or any other reasonably competent Exalted guy, could write some decent shrinking magic without any major complexity issues. Bonuses to stealth and Evasion, penalties to durability, Parry, and Strength. What's missing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881405#post881405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe broadest possible interpretation of shapeshifting contains a lot of things that either clash terribly with one another, or are rather overpowered or difficult to represent in this medium in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if there was something, but nothing is coming to mind right now. So it doesn't seem like any worse an issue for shapeshifting than it is for, say, elemental themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881405#post881405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI don't think the user interface, so to speak, is very well suited for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what that means. Are you agreeing with Saur Ops?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:28:56-07:00","id":881481,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.<br /> <br /> Actually, I kinda like the idea that Exalted Ant-Man would be more like an Exigent of a Cobbler-God than Yet More Lunar Shoehorning. A charm-set based around becoming tiny, doing craft-work rapidly when unseen, and not a heck of a lot else. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think Lunars DO need to cover Mystique, though, because the god(dess) most associated with having different faces IS Luna.<br /> <br /> Something more formless chaos-y would be easily enough pegged to a god with a portfolio involving watching the Wyld, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:30:37-07:00","id":881482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881447#post881447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, what Lunars were originally meant to be was bad. But don't take it from me, <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:where-it-all-went-wrong\" target=\"_blank\">take it from Holden</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is no, the approach that 1e had was terrible, on account of no one who was hired wanted to really work on it. I've already read that page many times, thanks, I know what it says. 2e followed it up with a tepid, retiring approach that didn't try to take what would have been an easy road toward fixing the problems, and tried to make Lunars into something their inspiration never ran with. We got a Luna from Werewolf, and the Lunars need to follow suit on growing from that kernel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, but that's GURPS. I think that I, or any other reasonably competent Exalted guy, could write some decent shrinking magic without any major complexity issues. Bonuses to stealth and Evasion, penalties to durability, Parry, and Strength. What's missing? </div> </div> </div>Coherence. Animalistic shapeshifters don't necessarily just shrink themselves down; again, they are not fucking Ant-Man, or Mystique, or Colossus, or The Thing From Another World. They are not blank templates to apply any special effects to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if there was something, but nothing is coming to mind right now. So it doesn't seem like any worse an issue for shapeshifting than it is for, say, elemental themes. </div> </div> </div>Elemental themes tend to nail things down a lot more than &quot;become anything else, alter shape in any way you see fit&quot;. They do things in certain and definite ways, even when operating on a more allegorical level. Being able to turn into a table or shoggoth would be to Lunars like Dragon-Blooded getting Aspects that line up with elements from the periodic table. It's not playing along with the theme of the character type, it's not keeping the feel of the setting, and it doesn't make the splats better, it just introduces a confusing inclusion of details that tries to knock the inspiration points out and replace them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:38:26-07:00","id":881486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881482#post881482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coherence. Animalistic shapeshifters don't necessarily just shrink themselves down; again, they are not fucking Ant-Man, or Mystique, or Colossus, or The Thing From Another World. They are not blank templates to apply any special effects to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Size-changing doesn't seem out of scope for Lunars, IMO. It's bodily and Attribute-focused in a fairly direct way, it's very straightforwardly physical in a way that doesn't compromise the identity of the character or come off as weird and spooky, and it's easy to model in the game using animal traits. I think Ant-man scale (or Attack on Titan scale) would be overkill, but something that lets a Lunar halve or double their height seems entirely within-theme to me, given that Lunars are likely to also have Charms that do things like make them more attractive, change their physical characteristics, and close wounds like the T-1000, none of which are in the bailiwick of animal shapeshifting. DBT already makes you bigger, even if your animal form is a mouse.<br /> <br /> It's on the periphery, so I wouldn't be surprised <i>not</i> to get it, but I certainly wouldn't cry foul if we did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T22:36:27-07:00","id":881521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881482#post881482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is no, the approach that 1e had was terrible, on account of no one who was hired wanted to really work on it. I've already read that page many times, thanks, I know what it says. 2e followed it up with a tepid, retiring approach that didn't try to take what would have been an easy road toward fixing the problems, and tried to make Lunars into something their inspiration never ran with. We got a Luna from Werewolf, and the Lunars need to follow suit on growing from that kernel.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to go. But to pretend that emulating Werewolf is the only workable path is just silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881482#post881482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coherence. Animalistic shapeshifters don't necessarily just shrink themselves down; again, they are not fucking Ant-Man, or Mystique, or Colossus, or The Thing From Another World. They are not blank templates to apply any special effects to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a separate disagreement. You think they should be specifically animalistic shapeshifters, I get that, but that has nothing to do with my response to your claim that shrinking is hard to handle mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881482#post881482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental themes tend to nail things down a lot more than &quot;become anything else, alter shape in any way you see fit&quot;. They do things in certain and definite ways, even when operating on a more allegorical level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is is just untrue. Elemental themes nail down almost nothing. They're incredibly broad. In fact, I think I could come up with about as many different Charms for any one element as for shapeshifting in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T23:13:56-07:00","id":881541,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Size-changing doesn't seem out of scope for Lunars, IMO. It's bodily and Attribute-focused in a fairly direct way, it's very straightforwardly physical in a way that doesn't compromise the identity of the character or come off as weird and spooky, and it's easy to model in the game using animal traits. I think Ant-man scale (or Attack on Titan scale) would be overkill, but something that lets a Lunar halve or double their height seems entirely within-theme to me, given that Lunars are likely to also have Charms that do things like make them more attractive, change their physical characteristics, and close wounds like the T-1000, none of which are in the bailiwick of animal shapeshifting. DBT already makes you bigger, even if your animal form is a mouse.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's on the periphery, so I wouldn't be surprised </span></span></span><i>not</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to get it, but I certainly wouldn't cry foul if we did.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That tends to devalue turning into smaller forms. Leave it to spirit Charms. Also, their healing isn't like T-1000, and they aren't made of amorphous liquid metal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881521#post881521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's one way to go. But to pretend that emulating Werewolf is the only workable path is just silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emulating isn't the term I'd use. Like I said, it uses it as an essential kernel of inspiration. Moving far away from the thesis of Lunars does no good for the Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a separate disagreement. You think they should be specifically animalistic shapeshifters, I get that, but that has nothing to do with my response to your claim that shrinking is hard to handle mechanically. </div> </div> </div>More importantly, the developers think that. As to the mechanical complexity, okay, maybe it can be written away easily. That still leaves the thematic clash; Ant-Man is just some guy in shrinking suit. Lunars are meant to change into different things, not differently-sized renditions of the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think this is is just untrue. Elemental themes nail down almost nothing. They're incredibly broad. In fact, I think I could come up with about as many different Charms for any one element as for shapeshifting in general. </div> </div> </div>That'd be hard, since general shapeshifting would by necessity subsume many of the elemental powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T23:39:29-07:00","id":881551,"title":"","content":"What thesis?<br /> <br /> Lunars haven't had a thesis, unless you count &quot;barbarian Exalted&quot;. The whole question is about how to give them one.<br /> <br /> Not sure what you mean by that last bit. Even if you consider turning into smoke (and the like) to be part of &quot;shapeshifting in general&quot; (I wouldn't, but I guess it's debatable), changing your own body is only a small corner of what elemental magic can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T02:47:51-07:00","id":881615,"title":"","content":"Heh. This thread actually got a chuckle out of me. When someone wants to narrow down Solars a bit from basically being like 90% of every single possible character type, the forum cries foul. When someone wants to expand Lunars a little bit beyond dudes what turn into animals, the forum cries foul.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my personal thought is that yes, it makes perfect sense for the Exalts that focus around modifying their own physical form to be able to make themselves smaller while remaining themselves, but no, we are probably not going to actually get it in canon, and will need to homebrew it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 05-04-2016, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:16:39-07:00","id":881651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, what Lunars were originally meant to be was bad.</div> </div> </div> </div> The part about writing with a bias has issues. Holden has also said, more recently, that there were parts being very specific about what kinds of shapeshifters Lunars are that they're taking a lot of cues from, and that one of the Second Edition weaknesses was having no mandate or guideline as to a coherent alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:31:00-07:00","id":881659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">any worse an issue for shapeshifting than it is for, say, elemental themes.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Dragon Blooded shouldn't have everything related to elemental themes either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:44:27-07:00","id":881663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881615#post881615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. This thread actually got a chuckle out of me. When someone wants to narrow down Solars a bit from basically being like 90% of every single possible character type, the forum cries foul. When someone wants to expand Lunars a little bit beyond dudes what turn into animals, the forum cries foul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure this observation of your is without any kind of bias whatsoever about the Exalted's forum and Solar ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:10:48-07:00","id":881667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881663#post881663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure this observation of your is without any kind of bias whatsoever about the Exalted's forum and Solar ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. I've been in this forum entirely too long and have clashed with too many viewpoints and had my thoughts dismissed and called badwrong entirely too many times to not have biases about it. <br /> <br /> Still pretty sure that the way the threads tend to crumble does tend to happen along those lines. When people suggest ideas for narrow-focusing the Solars, the prevailing argument is always against doing so. But at the same time, ideas for widening Lunars or Abyssals tend to be met with accusations of missing the point or diluting the splats into nothingness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:31:02-07:00","id":881679,"title":"","content":"I think shrinking Lunars could be implimented in a way that builds upon the ability to turn into small animals rather than rendering it obsolete or so readily accessable that people will be whining that the setting doesn't make sense because Cathak Cainan hasn't been killed by a Lunar in his soup yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:34:32-07:00","id":881684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881541#post881541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That tends to devalue turning into smaller forms. Leave it to spirit Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I say &quot;about half size or double&quot; as the limit of where I still consider it potentially Lunar-y (though I could see about a third or triple, at the outside range). At that size, I don't feel you're seriously devaluing smaller forms, particularly given that they tend to have their own powers and be far, far less conspicuous than a dwarf human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, their healing isn't like T-1000, and they aren't made of amorphous liquid metal. </div> </div> </div>&quot;You injure them and the wound just flows closed instantly&quot; is what I was going for -- not the clearest metaphor, but I couldn't think of a better one. They're not literally made of liquid metal, but you can absolutely do the shotgun scene from T2 with a Stamina-focused Lunar, it's just that there will be blood. My point is that it's clearly a power related from shapeshifting, but not from animal shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> In addition to straightforward Attribute charms, it seems likely that Lunars are will have shapeshifting charms in this game, since the only reason they didn't have more or these historically was charmshare. Some of these will be like 2e's Knacks in that they just straightforwardly enhance your existing shapeshifting ability, but others are probably just going to, you know, shift their shape. Stapling an animal metaphor to <i>all</i> those charms would be kind of weird, IMO. Lunars have always had <i>some </i>non-animal shapeshifting, even in cases where animal shapeshifting could theoretically accomplish something similar, and it seems likely that they always will. The only real question is what is within that scope. I'll leave that to the developers, but Solars got broadened an <i>awful</i> lot in 3e, so I would not be surprised to see every splat get some things that we wouldn't traditionally have seen going to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:50:32-07:00","id":881783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881684#post881684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You injure them and the wound just flows closed instantly&quot; is what I was going for -- not the clearest metaphor, but I couldn't think of a better one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, werewolves? Werewolves that are shown to heal back from most injuries so quickly that it seems like they were never injured? Because flesh isn't slowly flowing back when you use the fast healing Charms, it was basically that you see someone messed up badly, and then in the space of less than a second, they're standing back up and looking much better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're not literally made of liquid metal, but you can absolutely do the shotgun scene from T2 with a Stamina-focused Lunar, it's just that there will be blood. My point is that it's clearly a power related from shapeshifting, but not from animal shapeshifting. </div> </div> </div>It's another facet of Lunars, primal spiritual connections, that goes hand in hand with being inspired by W:tA, wherein you healed very quickly on account of being half-spirit (which has different connotations in that game, since in it, unlike Exalted, the god <i>is</i> the river). Even just one health level is a huge change that can go from on the brink of death to walking around, with some difficulty if you don't have a really high pain tolerance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition to straightforward Attribute charms, it seems likely that Lunars are will have shapeshifting charms in this game, since the only reason they didn't have more or these historically was charmshare. Some of these will be like 2e's Knacks in that they just straightforwardly enhance your existing shapeshifting ability, but others are probably just going to, you know, shift their shape. Stapling an animal metaphor to <i>all</i> those charms would be kind of weird, IMO. Lunars have always had <i>some </i>non-animal shapeshifting, even in cases where animal shapeshifting could theoretically accomplish something similar, and it seems likely that they always will. The only real question is what is within that scope. I'll leave that to the developers, but Solars got broadened an <i>awful</i> lot in 3e, so I would not be surprised to see every splat get some things that we wouldn't traditionally have seen going to them. </div> </div> </div>The only other thing I can think of as non-animal in the shapeshifting department are the things that allow you to reshape objects, and they felt weird. Also, 1e required you to smear your blood on anything you wanted to change, with very limited results. I suppose Tool-Hand Technique might also count, but who knows if that's actually going to get in, as opposed to passed off to some other type of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:56:32-07:00","id":881787,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Blankity-Blank Splat will cover all these other Shapeshifting Options?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:58:34-07:00","id":881788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881787#post881787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Blankity-Blank Splat will cover all these other Shapeshifting Options?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt we'd get everything that was removed in one splat. Lunars have two to cover the overflow, from what we've heard, and that still might leave room for more. It was an awful lot of stuff to heap on, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:00:59-07:00","id":881793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881788#post881788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt we'd get everything that was removed in one splat. Lunars have two to cover the overflow, from what we've heard, and that still might leave room for more. It was an awful lot of stuff to heap on, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I doubt we are going to get Odo, but maybe Mystique?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:32:05-07:00","id":881823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881788#post881788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt we'd get everything that was removed in one splat. Lunars have two to cover the overflow, from what we've heard, and that still might leave room for more. It was an awful lot of stuff to heap on, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff like Spreading the Wyld Roots and Blinking Eye of Chaos are almost certainly traveling into the Getimian Charmset.<br /> <br /> Stuff like Monkey Arm Style and Weapon-Trapping Body Dominion seem to have gone to the Liminal Charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:55:42-07:00","id":881854,"title":"","content":"Yes, Lunars shrink, particularly when swimming or it's cold out STOP JUDGING ME JADE FOX I'M A GROWER NOT A SHOWER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:23:59-07:00","id":881950,"title":"","content":"I will admit to a certain bias regarding this subject specifically, for anybody, because I find shrinking to be very silly. <br /> <br /> Whether it's an ability or an affliction, the moment you juxtapose a miniature person against anybody else, or go through a kitschy scene of somebody wandering around normal household items that are <i>hilariously</i> oversized, it takes me out of it.<br /> <br /> Ant-Man, the film, has a few exceptional things going for it that make that less of a distraction, but generally, the image of somebody sneaking around like a Borrower or being trapped inside of a jar or having a life-or-death struggle with an ant is just too goofy for my tastes.<br /> <br /> (Note this doesn't actually apply to the Borrowers, since there's a charm to the detail of them being that size all the time, and having an entire lifestyle built around it. Especially when it's in a Studio Ghibli story.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:07:30-07:00","id":882145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881788#post881788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt we'd get everything that was removed in one splat. Lunars have two to cover the overflow, from what we've heard, and that still might leave room for more. It was an awful lot of stuff to heap on, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis on &quot;awful.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:14:28-07:00","id":882220,"title":"","content":"Canonical Lunars for Ex3 seem more focused on becoming animals or people, based on the Antagonist section write-up. So in terms of doing size-but-not-shape-changing, you're probably going to want to go with a Sorcerous Working, assuming you care about what is canoncally appropriate.<br /> Somewhat off-topic... I don't get all the negativity about the notion of shrinking in an RPG. Fridge logic is highly subjective and most fantastic settings suffer for applying that kind of nitpicking. Bookkeeping... I mean, I don't know about you, but I'm already using a spreadsheet to track combats. We currently have tiny and legendary size merits, so the stat scaling issue is already present.<br /> Related, I don't see how an infiltration Lunar is in any way distinct from a Mystique type shapeshifter. Base concept, she turns into specific other people. That's it. I'm not a big expy fan so I wouldn't especially want a direct port, but it's hard for me to see how she and the infiltrating Lunar are not cut from similar cloth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11647-gargoyle","name":"Gargoyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:36:10-07:00","id":882247,"title":"","content":"The significance of Mystique isn't around Lunars not being able to turn into people, but about Lunars as face-stealers.<br /> <br /> Which is something that applies to the animals as well. Really, to the extent that disliking comparisons to Animorphs has any credibility, that's another thing that distinguishes Lunars from them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T15:04:55-07:00","id":882266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gargoyle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882220#post882220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonical Lunars for Ex3 seem more focused on becoming animals or people, based on the Antagonist section write-up. So in terms of doing size-but-not-shape-changing, you're probably going to want to go with a Sorcerous Working, assuming you care about what is canoncally appropriate.<br /> Somewhat off-topic... I don't get all the negativity about the notion of shrinking in an RPG. Fridge logic is highly subjective and most fantastic settings suffer for applying that kind of nitpicking. Bookkeeping... I mean, I don't know about you, but I'm already using a spreadsheet to track combats. We currently have tiny and legendary size merits, so the stat scaling issue is already present.<br /> Related, I don't see how an infiltration Lunar is in any way distinct from a Mystique type shapeshifter. Base concept, she turns into specific other people. That's it. I'm not a big expy fan so I wouldn't especially want a direct port, but it's hard for me to see how she and the infiltrating Lunar are not cut from similar cloth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because that's the only thing she does. Lunars have their own stuff, and intersect with Mystique tangentially at this point. But they have a lot of other stuff that makes them very much not like Mystique, so it'd be an error to mistake her for an example of a Lunar, unless you were willing to make a number of changes and adaptations to bring her in line with all of the other bits of the Lunar package.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:07:13-07:00","id":882392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881783#post881783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, werewolves? Werewolves that are shown to heal back from most injuries so quickly that it seems like they were never injured? Because flesh isn't slowly flowing back when you use the fast healing Charms, it was basically that you see someone messed up badly, and then in the space of less than a second, they're standing back up and looking much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was never really a part of the werewolf mythos so much as a part of Werewolf: the Apocalypse specifically, was it? Apocalypse werewolves can also turn into larger humanoids, and most of their powers weren't really animal shapeshifting in the first place, so I don't know how much that route actually gets you, but for what it's worth I am pretty sure both were meant to be able to model flesh visibly flowing back together and reknitting at the high end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881783#post881783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only other thing I can think of as non-animal in the shapeshifting department are the things that allow you to reshape objects, and they felt weird. Also, 1e required you to smear your blood on anything you wanted to change, with very limited results. I suppose Tool-Hand Technique might also count, but who knows if that's actually going to get in, as opposed to passed off to some other type of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have or 1e Lunars or remember it well enough to say offhand, but 2e had those charms (which did, admittedly, feel weird), the super healing, Perfect Symmetry, and Flowing Body Evasion.<br /> In Knacks they also had the Dhalsim thing, though, and they had the ability to change sex and physical characteristics.<br /> <br /> I actually tend to agree that a lot of the Lunar powers for changing <i>other</i> things and doing flowy-stretchy type effects seem a little weird. My rubric for Lunars is, &quot;would this power make sense for a primal, Attribute-oriented shapeshifter as conceptualized by Homer?&quot; (Assume you explained Attributes and Abilities to Homer, but didn't tell him about airplanes or anything.) For size-changing, the answer is yes. It's meat-and-potatoes ancient-world shapeshifter stuff, and it seems a lot closer to the heart of Lunar themes than a lot of things that Lunars <i>already</i> do. Also, of course, Lunars can <i>already</i> take the form of a person who's already giant or tiny, they just have to eat them first. So if being a giant or tiny person were totally inappropriate for Lunars, the ship has sailed.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not as invested in it as the amount I've posted here might lead you to presume -- either option is fine with me in practice. I just find the idea that it's hugely athematic for Lunars to be peculiar. It's as much of a worldly, mythically appropriate-ancient-world shapeshifting power as you can get, which seems to me like the place Lunars are coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:22:43-07:00","id":882401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882392#post882392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was never really a part of the werewolf mythos so much as a part of Werewolf: the Apocalypse specifically, was it? Apocalypse werewolves can also turn into larger humanoids, and most of their powers weren't really animal shapeshifting in the first place, so I don't know how much that route actually gets you, but for what it's worth I am pretty sure both were meant to be able to model flesh visibly flowing back together and reknitting at the high end.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then, if you completely destroy T-1000's material, it's out of mass, either losing, say, a limb, or else having to redistribute its total mass. A Lunar just grows new tissues where necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't have or 1e Lunars or remember it well enough to say offhand, but 2e had those charms (which did, admittedly, feel weird), the super healing, Perfect Symmetry, and Flowing Body Evasion.<br /> In Knacks they also had the Dhalsim thing, though, and they had the ability to change sex and physical characteristics.<br /> <br /> I actually tend to agree that a lot of the Lunar powers for changing <i>other</i> things and doing flowy-stretchy type effects seem a little weird. My rubric for Lunars is, &quot;would this power make sense for a primal, Attribute-oriented shapeshifter as conceptualized by Homer?&quot; (Assume you explained Attributes and Abilities to Homer, but didn't tell him about airplanes or anything.) For size-changing, the answer is yes. It's meat-and-potatoes ancient-world shapeshifter stuff, and it seems a lot closer to the heart of Lunar themes than a lot of things that Lunars <i>already</i> do. Also, of course, Lunars can <i>already</i> take the form of a person who's already giant or tiny, they just have to eat them first. So if being a giant or tiny person were totally inappropriate for Lunars, the ship has sailed.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not as invested in it as the amount I've posted here might lead you to presume -- either option is fine with me in practice. I just find the idea that it's hugely athematic for Lunars to be peculiar. It's as much of a worldly, mythically appropriate-ancient-world shapeshifting power as you can get, which seems to me like the place Lunars are coming from. </div> </div> </div>When a Lunar turns into a giant or tiny person, they change into that particular person. It's a bit different than compacting or expanding the form of something else because some other form is smaller or larger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:45:17-07:00","id":882409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882401#post882401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Lunar turns into a giant or tiny person, they change into that particular person. It's a bit different than compacting or expanding the form of something else because some other form is smaller or larger.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a <i>bit</i> different, agreed, but it seems like whatever damage is done to the motif of Lunars as animal shapeshifters who are incentivized to use animal forms is not done in that bit of difference.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think we've staked out our territory pretty well here. Let's set up a demilitarized zone in the middle and compete to see who can build the better economy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:46:46-07:00","id":882411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882392#post882392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, of course, Lunars can <i>already</i> take the form of a person who's already giant or tiny, they just have to eat them first. So if being a giant or tiny person were totally inappropriate for Lunars, the ship has sailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCreation probably doesn't have people the size on ants.<br /> <br /> Speaking of turning into people below the height of an average human adult...<br /> <br /> I know there are technical advantages to being of a stature smaller than would be typical for an adult, since it's part of the basis for child labour involving things like mining or ship breaking, and I know the physique of an adult with dwarfism is not equivalent to that of a child, so I'm wondering; in situations where assuming a small human size is warranted, would the shape of a human with dwarfism logically fulfil similar requirements to that of a child?<br /> <br /> On that note, I would find the capacity for a Lunar to transform into a child or dwarf version of themselves to be fitting, in keeping with existing powers to modify appearance without transforming entirely into new people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:56:56-07:00","id":882423,"title":"","content":"I don't think regeneration from injury has much of anything to do with shapeshifting, so it's not really related to the limits of Lunar shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Would I picture it as something like wounds instantly closing up? Ehhh... maybe? Even if that was the case, I'd feel that the association with the T-1000 would be purely cosmetic. It helps that Creation doesn't have shotguns, so the question of how it looks when a gaping hole in a Lunar closes doesn't feel like it needs to come up.<br /> <br /> I think Lunar regeneration magic is justified by their image of powerful, stubborn endurance, and the sublime quality of their divine bodies, not the shapeshifting. It doesn't need to have to do with Werewolf (even though I think it attributes regeneration mostly to Rage as well).<br /> <br /> (Although, as far as I understand it, any werewolf lore that supposes special materials required to wound or kill them supposes some kind of enhanced hardiness or healing as a matter of course. I know a couple of properties that attribute regeneration to werewolves, but they post date the first publication of Apocalypse, so I couldn't say if they were being influenced by the introduction of the idea to the popular consciousness beforehand)<br /> <br /> I think the significance in refuting the whole T-1000 is less about regeneration and more about being able to turn into a puddle that can freely shape itself into simple shapes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:08:47-07:00","id":882430,"title":"","content":"Is something fun?<br /> Then Lunars can't do it.<br /> <br /> That's what I'm taking away from this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:20:29-07:00","id":882443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882411#post882411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCreation probably doesn't have people the size on ants.</div> </div> </div> </div>We weren't arguing about size changing that dramatic! (Yes, that was what the OP was asking about, but that's what happens if you don't babysit your thread. Welcome to the jungle!)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:02:43-07:00","id":882591,"title":"","content":"Oh, so Creation has thematic space for heroin pissing sauropods and perky SR-71s, and rivers what flow uphill, but there's just no room for an expy of Lilliput and Blefuscu. I mean honestly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:48:02-07:00","id":882739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882591#post882591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so Creation has thematic space for heroin pissing sauropods and perky SR-71s, and rivers what flow uphill, but there's just no room for an expy of Lilliput and Blefuscu.</div> </div> </div> </div>An animal having urine with useful products in it is nowhere near as whimsical as a society of tiny people.<br /> <br /> Rivers that flow uphill is just... nothing. That's like citing the existence of coloured lights as a basis for adding whatever nonsense, it's so insignificant.<br /> <br /> Not everything fits into the same setting.<br /> <br /> Beasts of resplendent liquid fits because it already has dinosaurs and magically modified life and a background of economic basis in the ancient super civilisation.<br /> <br /> The Five-Metal Shrike fits because it's a remnant of an ancient civilization established to have incomprehensible and occasionally rogue superweapons.<br /> <br /> The River of Tears fits because gigantic uncanny civil engineering projects are a thing associated with unimaginably powerful precursors ever since the pyramids.<br /> <br /> How do your tiny people fit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882430#post882430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is something fun?<br /> Then Lunars can't do it.<br /> <br /> That's what I'm taking away from this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting into humans and animals is fun. I've particularly always liked the idea of a Lunar turning into a rat and having a scene like Remy scurrying around the crawlspaces of Paris, except where Paris is a Dynast's manse, and they overhear all kinds of lucrative plans and secrets.<br /> <br /> Lunars should shapeshift into people and animals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-05-2016, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:50:30-07:00","id":882740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882443#post882443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We weren't arguing about size changing that dramatic!</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I not cover that? With the whole extended digression about people with dwarfism and children? I thought I did; that was why I bothered bringing it up and putting it in the same post.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could have been explicit with my point of not equating turning into a shorter natural human being really constituting shrinking as most people would use the term when discussing a fantasy property.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:33:07-07:00","id":882766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881823#post881823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff like Spreading the Wyld Roots and Blinking Eye of Chaos are almost certainly traveling into the Getimian Charmset.<br /> <br /> Stuff like Monkey Arm Style and Weapon-Trapping Body Dominion seem to have gone to the Liminal Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also see a splat that more readily takes up the whole turning into supernatural creatures with their own essence based powers by limiting their ability to accquire new forms on the fly, thus making the limited number they have more like a specialised toolkit than raiding someone else's stuff for even more power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-05-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:49:55-07:00","id":882775,"title":"","content":"Something like the limitations of the Solar Charms to allow them to acquire more Charms, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:18:55-07:00","id":882844,"title":"","content":"Why would turning into an ant-sized human be more useful than turning into an actual ant? The Lunar can use a Charm to retain his strength even in an ant's form; Second Edition had Internal Form Mastery for carrying your Dexterity over into unDexterous forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T08:36:19-07:00","id":882893,"title":"","content":"It sounds like it boils down to what the vision for Lunars is. Are they limited to being &quot;the animal Exalted,&quot; or is that merely their starting point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:54:03-07:00","id":882943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882893#post882893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like it boils down to what the vision for Lunars is. Are they limited to being &quot;the animal Exalted,&quot; or is that merely their starting point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Abyssal Exalted are the &quot;ghost/vampire Exalted&quot;. Are ghosts just their starting point before they go on to emulate and control gods and demons and other spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:04:55-07:00","id":883032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882893#post882893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like it boils down to what the vision for Lunars is. Are they limited to being &quot;the animal Exalted,&quot; or is that merely their starting point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel framing the subject like this contains some loaded language, whether inadvertently or not.<br /> <br /> For one thing, I wouldn't think of Lunars not turning into many things beyond animals, and having a lot of Charms that reference mythic beast concepts, to render them as animal Exalted. Really, it would be a lot like reductively referring to Solars as &quot;the human Exalted&quot;<br /> <br /> I think with Lunars, it's a matter of having a theme or image to which the animal stuff is a component or subordinate, similar to how Lawgivers place the sun first while being largely expressed in culture and folk hero skills and having basically no sun powers.<br /> <br /> That's the argument for keeping them focused on the therianthropy. The argument against some of the others is when they're framed in terms of &quot;animals as a starting point&quot;, since I think treating something as a starting point that you graduate from... I don't find it to be the best as game design, because if people are chomping at the bit to move on from it, then why bother including it, or if it gets fully elaborated on then it clashes with anything else that might rely on it as a starting point. As a matter of purely personal taste, I don't care for it, because I think the therinathropy stuff is interesting and fitting and deserves care and attention.<br /> <br /> On that subject:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=881615#post881615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone wants to narrow down Solars a bit from basically being like 90% of every single possible character type, the forum cries foul. When someone wants to expand Lunars a little bit beyond dudes what turn into animals, the forum cries foul.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes? Because one of those is at the core of the game, both in terms of gameplay function and setting, and so is designed to be more widely serviceable, while the other is designed for a more precise and focused result.<br /> <br /> I get why people would become attached to the focused thing and want it to be expanded, but I don't think it's a very good idea as a game design thing.<br /> <br /> There are also other qualities to Lunars specifically, such as the values of maintaining a measure of image consistency, both with themselves and with the genre they're contained in. That's a reason why even for Solars, with their versatility, there are things that are fundamentally out of bounds. I think that settings that cast their net too wide ultimately become rather shallow, and have a harder time being compelling to people. That's probably not an issue for the person who wants their pet issue attached to it, but it's an issue if the necessary customer base for something consists of more then that person.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:01:31-07:00","id":883236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882740#post882740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did I not cover that? With the whole extended digression about people with dwarfism and children? I thought I did; that was why I bothered bringing it up and putting it in the same post.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could have been explicit with my point of not equating turning into a shorter natural human being really constituting shrinking as most people would use the term when discussing a fantasy property.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>but, </i>but...if you knew that wasn't the argument I was making then why did you present your comment as a rebuttal to me? <span style=\"font-size:11px\">agh this thread.</span><br /> <br /> Anyway, as to the &quot;turning into a shorter person isn't really the same as shrinking&quot;, this is true. My point was that most potential issues with shrinking also apply to with turning into a different human of comparable size, so it would be best if people limited criticism only to the ones that don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:48:27-07:00","id":883347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882844#post882844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would turning into an ant-sized human be more useful than turning into an actual ant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thumbs, voice. Ability to converse with aforementioned Lilliputian expies, depending on how equipment works, being able to wear it. Though a mundane suit of armor would be just as useless to an ant sized person as an ant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T18:12:24-07:00","id":883356,"title":"","content":"My feeling on this is that it makes sense that a Lunar can do Mystique-things (provided they obtain the form with respectful amounts of ultra-violence or similar means, Lunars are survivors that take what they want, not blue amalgamations of plot-conveniant BS). That being said I would say shrinking=ok, ant man shrinking= not ok, EOE makes sense because you grow to be strong and have the downsides, you can shrink but you should be considerably weaker.<br /> Also why is there no love for small forms? Every Changing Moon character my old ST ever made had at least one bug form!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:16:04-07:00","id":883393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883236#post883236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>but, </i>but...if you knew that wasn't the argument I was making then why did you present your comment as a rebuttal to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I was addressing your point at the same time as snarking about the possibility that it's a digression from the subject under discussion.<br /> <br /> Still, since the subject has been digressed to:<br /> <br /> What would a theoretical society of tiny people bring to the setting, and to any given game? What can they offer to, and how do their issues concern, player characters? How can they relate to any society around them? What compels one to go down to their level?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:25:09-07:00","id":883399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883347#post883347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thumbs, voice. Ability to converse with aforementioned Lilliputian expies, depending on how equipment works, being able to wear it. Though a mundane suit of armor would be just as useless to an ant sized person as an ant.</div> </div> </div> </div>...at the size of an ant, thumbs and a human voice would probably be more of a liability than a useful feature. Besides, as an ant, the Lunar could rule over the Lilliputians like a formic acid-spewing god! Especially if we're talking bullet ants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:48:35-07:00","id":883482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882591#post882591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so Creation has thematic space for heroin pissing sauropods and perky SR-71s</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that these things will not be particularly prominent in 3e. (They never really were to begin with, really, certainly not the way an <i>entire type of Exalted</i> are. Having a mention of animals that excrete drugs in one book is not the same as, say, devoting an entire splatbook to animals that excrete drugs.)<br /> <br /> Lunars need a uniting theme with a clear mythological basis -- something that fits into a fantasy universe like Exalted. Playing the T-1000 doesn't work for that.<br /> <br /> (Now, there might be some room to bend their themes a bit in a few places, or to build on the core themes in ways that branch out away from them a bit, but at heart they're about stealing people's shapes and turning into animals.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-06-2016, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T22:49:42-07:00","id":883502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883393#post883393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> I was addressing your point at the same time as snarking about the possibility that it's a digression from the subject under discussion.<br /> <br /> Still, since the subject has been digressed to:<br /> <br /> What would a theoretical society of tiny people bring to the setting, and to any given game? What can they offer to, and how do their issues concern, player characters? How can they relate to any society around them? What compels one to go down to their level?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do they add to things?<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, you end up with a race that make useful allies as spies, assassins, scouts (they can train and ride ordinary birds) and potentially craftspeople (incredibly intricate clockwork, f'rex). You get to use faerie tales - literally, the ones about the tiny faerie folk - in your story, perhaps having the PCs have to figure out what is behind the &quot;curse&quot; laid upon a particular person/place (it's these tiny people bedevilling them). Just one of them as an orphan foundling can make for a compelling character.<br /> <br /> Their relative lack of physical power makes them vulnerable to exploitation by larger neighbours, so a society of them could well be militarized, oppressed, or otherwise in an interesting position relative to the rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> Their food needs are, if we want to get realistic, likely to be quite high; they'd need constant sugary food access to maintain their metabolisms - and such foods are delicacies to bigger folk, and thus again, a potential point of conflict.<br /> <br /> A travelling show of little people (with a bigger human running the show) can make for an interesting bit of local colour, and also make you wonder about exploitation.<br /> <br /> And, finally: they'd make an interesting PC, now wouldn't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:13:46-07:00","id":883620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883482#post883482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that these things will not be particularly prominent in 3e. (They never really were to begin with, really, certainly not the way an <i>entire type of Exalted</i> are. Having a mention of animals that excrete drugs in one book is not the same as, say, devoting an entire splatbook to animals that excrete drugs.)<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bOh, I don't know; they're kind of necessary to the widespread existence of the heroin traded so lucratively by the Guild, even if the source doesn't need to be mentioned every time a plot involving heroin comes up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883502#post883502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What do they add to things?<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, you end up with a race that make useful allies as spies, assassins, scouts (they can train and ride ordinary birds) and potentially craftspeople (incredibly intricate clockwork, f'rex). You get to use faerie tales - literally, the ones about the tiny faerie folk - in your story, perhaps having the PCs have to figure out what is behind the &quot;curse&quot; laid upon a particular person/place (it's these tiny people bedevilling them). Just one of them as an orphan foundling can make for a compelling character.<br /> <br /> Their relative lack of physical power makes them vulnerable to exploitation by larger neighbours, so a society of them could well be militarized, oppressed, or otherwise in an interesting position relative to the rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> Their food needs are, if we want to get realistic, likely to be quite high; they'd need constant sugary food access to maintain their metabolisms - and such foods are delicacies to bigger folk, and thus again, a potential point of conflict.<br /> <br /> A travelling show of little people (with a bigger human running the show) can make for an interesting bit of local colour, and also make you wonder about exploitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA lot of these sound like treating a group as a resource to be exploited by players first and a society consisting of people with meaningful lives and interesting stories second, something that's bad enough when it's done with normal humans.<br /> <br /> And if they're tiny faerie folk, it sounds like they should come from the Wyld. Indeed, I was actually thinking before that the Wyld is one of the few contexts in which I would find such a thing sensible, right down to how the Liliputians were initially designed as an elaborate social satire rather than a piece of world building.<br /> <br /> I wonder what some Sidereals would think if they came across a colony of Wyld creatures who were made by a raksha that fancied itself some of a wit for casting the divisions between Sidereal policies towards Solars as insignificant differences in fashion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:18:35-07:00","id":883624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883482#post883482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that these things will not be particularly prominent in 3e. (They never really were to begin with, really, certainly not the way an <i>entire type of Exalted</i> are. Having a mention of animals that excrete drugs in one book is not the same as, say, devoting an entire splatbook to animals that excrete drugs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever. One of the appealing aspects of Exalted is that it's a strange pulp fantasy setting. If the Devs choose not to bring those aspects back, I will be happy to find different goofy things distinct to Ex3 if need be. Either way, Creation will continue to be a weird, wild and wooly setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lunars need a uniting theme with a clear mythological basis -- something that fits into a fantasy universe like Exalted. Playing the T-1000 doesn't work for that.<br /> <br /> (Now, there might be some room to bend their themes a bit in a few places, or to build on the core themes in ways that branch out away from them a bit, but at heart they're about stealing people's shapes and turning into animals.) </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess that is true. It's not likes a prominent mythological figure that inspired a number of Lunar characteristics that changed his size as well as his shape. <a href=\"http://orig09.deviantart.net/5eb9/f/2012/056/f/d/commission_example___sun_wukong_by_wahay-d4qyzga.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Oh..wait.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 05-06-2016, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:40:48-07:00","id":883762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883624#post883624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess that is true. It's not likes a prominent mythological figure that inspired a number of Lunar characteristics that changed his size as well as his shape. <a href=\"http://orig09.deviantart.net/5eb9/f/2012/056/f/d/commission_example___sun_wukong_by_wahay-d4qyzga.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Oh..wait.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Superman is one of the inspirations for Solar Exalted, but there are a number of things they don't get from him.<br /> <br /> Achilles and Odysseus are inspirations for Solar Exalted, and yet Solars get to do a number of crazy things they never could.<br /> <br /> Taking inspiration from a thing doesn't mean slavishly copying it, especially because, in Exalted, Sun Wukong could easily be a Raksha noble, a demon, a god, a behemoth, a beastman Solar or Sidereal (as sorcery allows for forms of shapeshifting, and he is explicitly a sorceror).<br /> <br /> What worked for him doesn't always work for Lunar Exalted as a splat, just as what worked for Superman doesn't always work for Solar Exalted as a splat.<br /> <br /> But sorcerous workings (and stranger things) let Solars get laser-eyes and let Lunars shrink themselves without assuming the stolen forms of tiny creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T21:54:59-07:00","id":884368,"title":"","content":"<i>Edit: </i>eh, this post was too bitchy. gimme a sec, I'll post a cat instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/CUOelLX.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">sorted</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 05-07-2016, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:09:33-07:00","id":884380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=884368#post884368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was extremely unclear! Also, it seems bad form to snark about something and then do the same thing enthusiastically?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> It may be, and if so I apologise.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, engaging in discussion of people of below-average height was something I did motivated by a sense that doing nothing but snarking was highly unfair. My intent was to open with a minor joke, and then continue discussion in good faith. My caustic and oblique attitude has obviously detracted from that, which I regret, and shall also apologise for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, okay, I should elaborate on that a little: I don't see that as a relevant discussion to bring to the thread. It's not germane to the thread topic <i>or</i> to the digression I was having. Incremental derails are fair play, but you will need to find someone else to do that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That question was to the person or persons who <i>had</i> extended the topic to the assertion that my sense that tiny people aren't very fitting to the setting was flawed.<br /> <br /> Which may not be a topic I should contribute any more to, as I'm a bit worried I may just be obstinate about it regardless of any arguments made against me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:21:30-07:00","id":884386,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing about this thread is to see that a lot of people conceptualize shapeshifting really differently from me. Much of the reason I say &quot;sure why not&quot; toward it is that changing into animals and changing your own size are filed <i>right</i> next to one another in my mind in terms of &quot;types of shapeshifting&quot; -- I have them both indexed as core motifs of ancient mythological shapeshifters, based in what seemed to me to be a more intuitive, physical notion of shapeshifting uninformed by modern tropes on the subject. You do still have superheroes who do both, but it's very much &quot;classic old-school&quot; shapeshifting, which I felt was closer to the root of Lunar themes than direct animalism. I can't really defend that reading, Lunar themes being what they are, so that might also explain some of the difference of opinion.<br /> <br /> When I think of Lunars -- just personally -- I think of them as being thematically associated with ancient Greek monsters, recast through the lens of a person and possibly a protagonist. The animalism is there, but I see it more as a metaphor for frightening external forces rather than a core theme. Of course, Lunars have been all over the place and we all come to terms with them in our own way.<br /> <br /> (The reason I still come out leaning against Ant-Man scale is because I don't like Lunar shifting to be <i>surreal</i>, since they have a very worldly, hyperreal feel going on. At some point radical alterations in physical scale start to come unmoored from people's actual experience of the world in a way that I think is better suited to the Wyld, which is overtly surreal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:29:29-07:00","id":884392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=884386#post884386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing about this thread is to see that a lot of people conceptualize shapeshifting really differently from me. Much of the reason I say &amp;quot;sure why not&amp;quot; toward it is that changing into animals and changing your own size are filed <i>right</i> next to one another in my mind in terms of &amp;quot;types of shapeshifting&amp;quot; -- I have them both indexed as core motifs of ancient mythological shapeshifters, based in what seemed to me to be a more intuitive, physical notion of shapeshifting uninformed by modern tropes on the subject. You do still have superheroes who do both, but it's very much &amp;quot;classic old-school&amp;quot; shapeshifting, which I felt was closer to the root of Lunar themes than direct animalism. I can't really defend that reading, Lunar themes being what they are, so that might also explain some of the difference of opinion.<br /> <br /> When I think of Lunars -- just personally -- I think of them as being thematically associated with ancient Greek monsters, recast through the lens of a person and possibly a protagonist. The animalism is there, but I see it more as a metaphor for frightening external forces rather than a core theme. Of course, Lunars have been all over the place and we all come to terms with them in our own way.<br /> <br /> (The reason I still come out leaning against Ant-Man scale is because I don't like Lunar shifting to be <i>surreal</i>, since they have a very worldly, hyperreal feel going on. At some point radical alterations in physical scale start to come unmoored from people's actual experience of the world in a way that I think is better suited to the Wyld, which is overtly surreal.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with this, for me Lunar powers are supposed to be primal and unsettling, I always interpret Lunar powers as their bodies working in ways that would strike most people as wrong. Ant-man is just not that, if anything he is not nearly as horrific as he should be (which is my gripe with the powers of most comic book heroes). If I wanted a Lunar to change size I would look to Attack on Titan long before I looked at Ant-Man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:28:26-07:00","id":884463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=884386#post884386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing about this thread is to see that a lot of people conceptualize shapeshifting really differently from me. Much of the reason I say &quot;sure why not&quot; toward it is that changing into animals and changing your own size are filed <i>right</i> next to one another in my mind in terms of &quot;types of shapeshifting&quot; -- I have them both indexed as core motifs of ancient mythological shapeshifters, based in what seemed to me to be a more intuitive, physical notion of shapeshifting uninformed by modern tropes on the subject. You do still have superheroes who do both, but it's very much &quot;classic old-school&quot; shapeshifting, which I felt was closer to the root of Lunar themes than direct animalism. I can't really defend that reading, Lunar themes being what they are, so that might also explain some of the difference of opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that is part of where I'm coming from. To me, changing your own size is FAR more easily related to classic animal shapeshifters than stealing people's faces, which is a completely different bag of tricks that mostly goes on the spirit and/or evil magic side of the equation. So it just seems like &quot;...what the christ are you talking about?&quot; when people start crying that growing and shrinking powers is &quot;diluting their concept as therianthropes&quot; or whatever. Lunars are <i>already </i>diluted as is, because &quot;turning into animals&quot; and &quot;take people's faces&quot; have had minimal intersection! And this fits a whole fucking lot more anyway! If anything it's concentrating, not diluting!<br /> <br /> (Now, to be fully honest for a minute as an aside, not that I actually would <i>mind </i>diluting the thing a bunch. Like three quarters of all halfway known therianthrope myths live in an extremely, <i>extremely </i>limited narrative slot. I've never felt that therianthropy alone is anywhere near enough to sustain a full player splat that actually justifies its own wordcount. I've always wanted my Lunars to have more mystery to them, since the Moon has always been a symbol for the mystical, the changing, the knowably mysterious. A Lunar performer in my mind should be entirely capable of sitting down in a clearing of the forest under the full moon and playing Moonlight Sonata by tugging the actual moonlight rays like a harp. But I realize THAT kind of ethereality would be a dilution of the primal and physical therianthropy focus the devs want to go for, the same way or even more than all the face stealing is).<br /> <br /> But growing and shrinking? That's just another facet of the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 05-07-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T04:09:31-07:00","id":884524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883620#post883620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bA lot of these sound like treating a group as a resource to be exploited by players first and a society consisting of people with meaningful lives and interesting stories second, something that's bad enough when it's done with normal humans.<br /> <br /> And if they're tiny faerie folk, it sounds like they should come from the Wyld. Indeed, I was actually thinking before that the Wyld is one of the few contexts in which I would find such a thing sensible, right down to how the Liliputians were initially designed as an elaborate social satire rather than a piece of world building.<br /> <br /> I wonder what some Sidereals would think if they came across a colony of Wyld creatures who were made by a raksha that fancied itself some of a wit for casting the divisions between Sidereal policies towards Solars as insignificant differences in fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You asked for &quot;how is this relevant to players&quot; and then were surprised when I answered with the ways players (and, I'll note, *NPCs*, could take advantage of their existence???<br /> <br /> <br /> In-and-of-themselves, they'd be as interesting and meaningful as they were written to be. There's multiple possible points of origin (created in ancient days before the Exalts, created by the Exalts, came into existence as a byproduct of something someone was attempting, Raksha wit, sheer random chance on Wyld mutation, crawled out of the Well, someone's homunculi became true-breeding, Creation's Pinocchio was a tiny little finger puppet and finger puppette who got to live happily ever after, or maybe 'I dunno, they've always been there'), which have varying levels of potential interest, there's an awful lot of possibilities for attitude and culture (pick a random century and country and run with it)...<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, &quot;gold hat smurfs&quot; vs. &quot;bronze hat smurfs&quot;, fighting an eternal war on two tiny islands in a minor lake somewhere really does sound like the best option. Oh what a merry jape. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now you get the fun of dealing with a society of people created by the Fae to be intentionally super petty (and literally small-minded) and easily factionalised - yet potentially incredibly useful allies, if you can get them past their divisions and dissensions. How do they interact with gods, the underworld, fate... quite a lot to explore there too, really.<br /> <br /> ...damnit, I think I need to include these guys in my game. They serve as a perfect way to say &quot;no, seriously, Creation is full of weird shit, including stuff the GM throws in for the hell of it&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...oh my, and what happens when a tiny person falls for their Exalted saviour? Oh, what a difficulty-fraught romance that could be...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T04:53:16-07:00","id":884549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You asked for &quot;how is this relevant to players&quot; and then were surprised when I answered with the ways players</div> </div> </div> </div> I think my question may have been based on assumptions that felt very familiar to me but that I failed to state explicitly. To clarify; I think the better written societies in Exalted are ones that feel as though they existed prior to the presence of player characters, internally and with relations with neighbours, with fracture points based on an uncertain future that player characters can interact with. I think the weaker ones such as Chaya come across wholly as staging grounds for plot devices, which feel too contrived. When I asked &quot;what does this offer for players&quot;, my assumption is that players will first want to interact with those fracture points (not necessarily resolve them beneficially).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T05:53:22-07:00","id":884568,"title":"","content":"I can see a lot of people in this thread saying &quot;Lunars can't shrinking because tiny people are silly IMO&quot; and dressing that up in some sort of grand thesis for the Lunars and the setting as a whole when really just admit you think it looks silly man.<br /> <br /> I think shrinking looks pretty silly myself. It doesn't seem to fit the aesthetic of the game. But I've got no real issue with it, if it was there, then okay no biggie. I guess that IMO Lunar Shapeshifting should involve taking animal traits more than anything? So you can shapeshift into, say, a mouse! And that's tiny. And if you want to be big and scary, a Tyrant Lizard! All that stuff. Rather than a giant person or a tiny person, you turn into the relevant beastie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T06:30:53-07:00","id":884581,"title":"","content":"Has anybody besides me suggested that shrinking is silly? And have I suggested anything apart from it being silly, other than briefly suggesting at the beginning that it's something I think is fiddly in roleplaying games in general?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T06:52:52-07:00","id":884586,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'll admit that I'm mostly talking about your opinion here. But yeah I do think you're dressing up a simple point of aesthetic taste (which I'll even agree with!) as something more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T07:27:50-07:00","id":884602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=884549#post884549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think my question may have been based on assumptions that felt very familiar to me but that I failed to state explicitly. To clarify; I think the better written societies in Exalted are ones that feel as though they existed prior to the presence of player characters, internally and with relations with neighbours, with fracture points based on an uncertain future that player characters can interact with. I think the weaker ones such as Chaya come across wholly as staging grounds for plot devices, which feel too contrived. When I asked &quot;what does this offer for players&quot;, my assumption is that players will first want to interact with those fracture points (not necessarily resolve them beneficially).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically the complete opposite of &quot;what does this offer for players&quot;.<br /> <br /> It is, in fact, &quot;what do they offer in the way of world-building that makes them feel like they exist independent to - and prior to the entrance of - the players&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> Better written, yes, but better written by NOT being about &quot;what does this offer for players&quot;; it is much easier to write THAT kind of place by not thinking about players and instead writing a place that is real(istic) and full of your best ideas and then coming back later and trimming it a little to make sure it's not UNplayable. <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, thank you for trying to explain, but for, it's like you're saying &quot;what I meant when I said 'paint it black' was that I wanted it painted white&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T10:01:24-07:00","id":884704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=883624#post883624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess that is true. It's not likes a prominent mythological figure that inspired a number of Lunar characteristics that changed his size as well as his shape. <a href=\"http://orig09.deviantart.net/5eb9/f/2012/056/f/d/commission_example___sun_wukong_by_wahay-d4qyzga.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Oh..wait.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Changing his size wasn't really his core power, though. (I mean, I guess he changed the size of his staff a lot, but that was more of an artifact.)<br /> <br /> And like I said, there's some room for wriggle room or to build on your themes in ways that branch out. If a Lunar is a master of turning into a huge ape, turning into an even <i>huger</i> ape is a reasonable extension of that, in the same sense that eg. creating things from nowhere via Words as Workshop Method isn't particularly central to being a Solar but can be a reasonable extension of Solar Craft.<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't want to say Lunars can <i>never</i> shrink -- you might be able to squeeze it somewhere into their powerset -- it's just not a core Lunar thing. If Lunars have eg. a clone-myself charm, they might get an upgrade that creates a lot of really small clones to rush about in order to complete a task quickly, but it would be a peripheral sort of upgrade. But it would probably be designed in a way that would reflect the fact that it's peripheral, making it at least a bit hard to play &quot;the guy who shrinks&quot; as your Lunar, in the same way that even if Solars get WaWM, it's hard to be &quot;the guy who conjures stuff from nowhere&quot; as your main concept when playing a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-07-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T10:36:09-07:00","id":884726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=884602#post884602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's basically the complete opposite of &quot;what does this offer for players&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... couple of things.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy questions were intended as basically components of a larger question; answering &quot;what do they offer players&quot; in isolation to all of the rest was not answering my question, and does not produce a result I would find useful to the game.<br /> <br /> The other thing is repeating my assertion that the thing to offer players in writing setting locations is something to play within.<br /> <br /> At that last White Elephant, when I was asked to write up a setting, that was something I struggled to realise; how to write a place to set games, rather than one that might just be interesting to read about because interesting things happened there are long time ago.<br /> <br /> The idea of gifting somebody with a setting that provides readily accessible assets did not even occur to me, because it's not how I conceive of what should be offered to players.<br /> <br /> I assume that, first and foremost, players want interesting stories about people, so I was asking what Liliputians offer to fulfil that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, thank you for trying to explain, but for, it's like you're saying &quot;what I meant when I said 'paint it black' was that I wanted it painted white&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's more like asking a person what they have to offer me and they start listing their assets and resources and naming numbers, when what I was looking for is a life partner.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:31:14-07:00","id":887197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=884704#post884704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't want to say Lunars can <i>never</i> shrink -- you might be able to squeeze it somewhere into their powerset -- it's just not a core Lunar thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I interpreted the topic of this thread to be, &quot;Can they do this at all?&quot; rather than to be, &quot;Is this a core function of their power suite?&quot;<br /> <br /> I would argue that it's something that not every Lunar should do, but that <u>a</u> Lunar might (and even multiple might). I could see it being a core thing for <u>a</u> Lunar who really liked something in that area. The mythical ability of Leviathan's protege, the Sea Monkey King, perhaps, to be any size he likes, and who has incorporated it into his own personal fighting style.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd see them starting from animal motifs, and only &quot;moving beyond&quot; them by expanding the notion of what an animal is. Especially when it overlaps heavily with their &quot;Fae Things&quot; theme(s).<br /> <br /> But by the same token, who's to say that the Lunar doesn't achieve shrinking by getting a Lilliputian Heart's Blood form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:32:32-07:00","id":887198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887197#post887197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I interpreted the topic of this thread to be, &quot;Can they do this at all?&quot; rather than to be, &quot;Is this a core function of their power suite?&quot;<br /> <br /> I would argue that it's something that not every Lunar should do, but that <u>a</u> Lunar might (and even multiple might). I could see it being a core thing for <u>a</u> Lunar who really liked something in that area. The mythical ability of Leviathan's protege, the Sea Monkey King, perhaps, to be any size he likes, and who has incorporated it into his own personal fighting style.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd see them starting from animal motifs, and only &quot;moving beyond&quot; them by expanding the notion of what an animal is. <b>Especially when it overlaps heavily with their &quot;Fae Things&quot; theme(s).</b><br /> <br /> But by the same token, who's to say that the Lunar doesn't achieve shrinking by getting a Lilliputian Heart's Blood form?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as we can tell, this is dead and gone. And good riddance, if so, because it never fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:40:37-07:00","id":887206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887198#post887198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as we can tell, this is dead and gone. And good riddance, if so, because it never fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't entirely disagree, but I do somewhat. I am glad it won't be a major theme such that we run into the question of what the Raksha are allowed to do without stepping on the &quot;real splat's&quot; toes. On the other hand, the Lunars-as-wardens-of-the-wyld has always been a cool aspect of them, to me. I don't think it should be all-encompassing, but the idea that their adaptive nature makes them ideally suited to hold back the Wyld and even lead the expeditions into it is a good space for them. Not the only space they should have, by any means, but it's a nice aspect to their schtick of contrasting civilization to untamed wilderness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:12:28-07:00","id":887228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887206#post887206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't entirely disagree, but I do somewhat. I am glad it won't be a major theme such that we run into the question of what the Raksha are allowed to do without stepping on the &quot;real splat's&quot; toes. On the other hand, the Lunars-as-wardens-of-the-wyld has always been a cool aspect of them, to me. I don't think it should be all-encompassing, but the idea that their adaptive nature makes them ideally suited to hold back the Wyld and even lead the expeditions into it is a good space for them. Not the only space they should have, by any means, but it's a nice aspect to their schtick of contrasting civilization to untamed wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld is not the wilderness, nor is it a force that any number of Lunars could hope to block as a living wall, much less numbering only under 400, most of whom have things to do that don't involve setting up shop far away from their enemies and getting extremely bored with the fact that there are no actual incursions of chaos like in the Contagion, which, by the way, no one could actually hold back, Lunar or otherwise.<br /> <br /> You've forced me to use an ear-worm weapon against you. When it comes to Lunars and Wyld connections, you really need to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kHue-HaXXzg\" target=\"_blank\">Let It Go</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T11:03:38-07:00","id":887307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887228#post887228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wyld is not the wilderness, nor is it a force that any number of Lunars could hope to block as a living wall, much less numbering only under 400, most of whom have things to do that don't involve setting up shop far away from their enemies and getting extremely bored with the fact that there are no actual incursions of chaos like in the Contagion, which, by the way, no one could actually hold back, Lunar or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I said &quot;a wall,&quot; I apologize; I was picturing more as patrolmen and scouts into it. They're the scouts and the point-men for incursions into the Wyld, and for targeted counter-assaults on Wyld incursions into Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887228#post887228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've forced me to use an ear-worm weapon against you. When it comes to Lunars and Wyld connections, you really need to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kHue-HaXXzg\" target=\"_blank\">Let It Go</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, at work, I cannot youtube. However, I do like that song; it does not have the dread effect on me that it does on others.<br /> <br /> Muhuhahahahahahaha.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T11:10:11-07:00","id":887314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887307#post887307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I said &quot;a wall,&quot; I apologize; I was picturing more as patrolmen and scouts into it. They're the scouts and the point-men for incursions into the Wyld, and for targeted counter-assaults on Wyld incursions into Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still too widely-distributed for any one Exalted to really have it as a thing (even the Dragon-Blooded lack the numbers to do so), still an aimless exercise in being away from where the action is and not influencing the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T11:59:13-07:00","id":887362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887314#post887314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still too widely-distributed for any one Exalted to really have it as a thing (even the Dragon-Blooded lack the numbers to do so), still an aimless exercise in being away from where the action is and not influencing the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first part may be true, but the second part shouldn't be. The Lunars exploring that story are the explorer-archetypes, the rangers, the hunters. They're the woodsmen who wield the axe that freed Red Riding Hood. They're the legendary monster in the jungle which keeps the village safe...but in fear of breaking its taboos. &quot;Where the action is&quot; depends a lot on the story being told. Not all of them must be about building kingdoms in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:13:42-07:00","id":887375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887362#post887362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first part may be true, but the second part shouldn't be. The Lunars exploring that story are the explorer-archetypes, the rangers, the hunters. They're the woodsmen who wield the axe that freed Red Riding Hood. They're the legendary monster in the jungle which keeps the village safe...but in fear of breaking its taboos. &quot;Where the action is&quot; depends a lot on the story being told. Not all of them must be about building kingdoms in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where the action is is in Creation. They don't build kingdoms, and I didn't say they did, but they are clashing with the other Exalted over where Creation is going to head. This is best done, again, by having them be inside Creation, and not out in the Wyld, or in Malfeas, or any other locale. Also, those archetypes? You're talking to me about raising up kingdoms being too out of it, but those roles, too, are not exactly in-line with what Lunars are. Maybe in the First Age, when they supported the Solars, but now? Now, they're the ones knocking at the door, and they're the wolf, not the woodsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:22:55-07:00","id":887386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887375#post887375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where the action is is in Creation. They don't build kingdoms, and I didn't say they did, but they are clashing with the other Exalted over where Creation is going to head. This is best done, again, by having them be inside Creation, and not out in the Wyld, or in Malfeas, or any other locale. Also, those archetypes? You're talking to me about raising up kingdoms being too out of it, but those roles, too, are not exactly in-line with what Lunars are. Maybe in the First Age, when they supported the Solars, but now? Now, they're the ones knocking at the door, and they're the wolf, not the woodsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why they can't be both.<br /> <br /> Regardless, not every game must focus on steering Creation into a new era. Of course many will! And Lunars should support telling those kinds of stories. But that doesn't mean they're the ONLY kind of story any given splat can be allowed to support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:32:58-07:00","id":887396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887386#post887386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why they can't be both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weight is far more on the BB wolf side than the woodsman side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless, not every game must focus on steering Creation into a new era. Of course many will! And Lunars should support telling those kinds of stories. But that doesn't mean they're the ONLY kind of story any given splat can be allowed to support. </div> </div> </div>Trying to bring about an end to the era of Dragon-Blooded control is a central urge to Lunars in EX3. It's the anchor they need after having been set adrift for two prior editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:53:16-07:00","id":887414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=887396#post887396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to bring about an end to the era of Dragon-Blooded control is a central urge to Lunars in EX3. It's the anchor they need after having been set adrift for two prior editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Glad you like it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T17:05:32-07:00","id":891450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882766#post882766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also see a splat that more readily takes up the whole turning into supernatural creatures with their own essence based powers by limiting their ability to accquire new forms on the fly, thus making the limited number they have more like a specialised toolkit than raiding someone else's stuff for even more power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further thoughts...<br /> There's also room for a new splat to pick up 2e Chimeraism where the risk of uncontrolled mutation and gradual loss of self is a result of their patron being a Great Old One or something rather than &quot;we broke our own Exaltations&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:09:20-07:00","id":891542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=882739#post882739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do your tiny people fit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Race of tiny people servants created to work inside ancient machines. Done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T23:31:21-07:00","id":891596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator 