":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:51:45-07:00","id":891776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891738#post891738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the sorcerer not just make smarter ants?</div> </div> </div> </div>And we've come full circle on the Ant-Man thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:29:05-07:00","id":891965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891598#post891598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the 2e Djala, all over again...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that's the joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891637#post891637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b&quot;Oh, we have an elaborate fantasy nonsense reason for existing, and have then just kind of putzed around uselessly for the thousand years since it became irrelevant I suppose.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: the Exalted. First Age ruins. All the other created races. Maybe humanity.<br /> <br /> People find their own uses after the things they were created for stop mattering. That's a thing, in this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:53:03-07:00","id":891982,"title":"","content":"If I had to throw an observation into here that unifies how Lunar shapeshifting works, I'd say they take the forms of others with the emphasis being on &quot;take.&quot; They literally start out by taking the forms of others by eating their hearts, and then later they can branch out into assuming only parts of the forms they take, and maybe taking forms via means other than fatal, the obvious ones being &quot;Tasting the target's blood in a non-fatal manner&quot; and &quot;Having sex with the target.&quot; I think John once proposed letting Lunars borrow someone's form by <i>doing a favor for them</i>, but even that's a function of &quot;You owe me, I'm taking your shape.&quot; There's also another branch of expansion there about taking someone else's form and idealizing it or extrapolating from it mythically, so you can become a super-gorilla or a titan-orca instead of just a regular gorilla or regular orca. I guess adjusting your own age or sexual characteristics falls into that?<br /> <br /> Lunars can't grow or shrink like Ant-Man because there's nothing like &quot;You, but really big/small&quot; for them to hook that face-stealing theme into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:55:28-07:00","id":891983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891637#post891637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b&quot;Oh, we have an elaborate fantasy nonsense reason for existing, and have then just kind of putzed around uselessly for the thousand years since it became irrelevant I suppose.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So like half the setting for most of Exalted's history? 'cause that pretty much sums up kind of a lot of Exalted's cosmology. Starting with literally the entire Underworld, which is in fact irrelevant by design in the setting history until it becomes relevant for a setting event (ie, the Deathlord offensive starting). And that not even getting into the smaller things. How many things even are there in the setting that, when stripped from the frills, basically read &quot;these things were created because of nonsense reason X, and now are there waiting in case your players want to interact with them&quot;. Because that includes a lot of the tail end of the Compass books. You have weird people with strange afflictions that then just spent millenia putzing around and being raiders to survive, unless the PCs interact with them. You have entire species of beasts literally created to do nothing but putz around inside tombs for millenia to guard them (Compass South, I seem to remember?) because they're there because they could be an interesting thing for the PCs to encounter. You have entire spirit genera with no other use than being a thing what sleeps under the earth for your players to encounter if they go delving. Heck, a lot of Masters of Jade was barely disguised weird plot hooks and interesting little oddities for players to latch on.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That's fine! That's in fact more than fine. An RPG setting <i>is </i>basically a collection of shit put there with a justification for the primary purpose of giving you plot hooks. A few tribes of little people struggling with life due to their tiny size is a perfectly valid thing to put into a setting. Definitely a thing that can catch players' attention, and there interesting thought to be had for a GM about how a culture of people thirty centimeters tall would shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:01:39-07:00","id":891990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891983#post891983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So like half the setting for most of Exalted's history? 'cause that pretty much sums up kind of a lot of Exalted's cosmology. Starting with literally the entire Underworld, which is in fact irrelevant by design in the setting history until it becomes relevant for a setting event (ie, the Deathlord offensive starting). And that not even getting into the smaller things. How many things even are there in the setting that, when stripped from the frills, basically read &quot;these things were created because of nonsense reason X, and now are there waiting in case your players want to interact with them&quot;. Because that includes a lot of the tail end of the Compass books. You have weird people with strange afflictions that then just spent millenia putzing around and being raiders to survive, unless the PCs interact with them. You have entire species of beasts literally created to do nothing but putz around inside tombs for millenia to guard them (Compass South, I seem to remember?) because they're there because they could be an interesting thing for the PCs to encounter. You have entire spirit genera with no other use than being a thing what sleeps under the earth for your players to encounter if they go delving. Heck, a lot of Masters of Jade was barely disguised weird plot hooks and interesting little oddities for players to latch on.<br /> <br /> And you know what? That's fine! That's in fact more than fine. An RPG setting <i>is </i>basically a collection of shit put there with a justification for the primary purpose of giving you plot hooks. A few tribes of little people struggling with life due to their tiny size is a perfectly valid thing to put into a setting. Definitely a thing that can catch players' attention, and there interesting thought to be had for a GM about how a culture of people thirty centimeters tall would shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't all of the &quot;this exists for a silly reason from the First Age, now the rubes think it's impressive&quot; the kind of tone they're not actually aiming for anymore? Because you just cited an awful lot of second edition fluff, and nearly all of it is on probation, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:04:41-07:00","id":892086,"title":"","content":"I'm anti ant-sized humans because the 1-5 scale fails miserably to do it justice and in this game, human normally = Exaltation.<br /> I'm okay with a shapeshifter using size altering powers in creative ways but the 2mm tall Dawn Caste crushing everything in their path seems really, really dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:14:28-07:00","id":892095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892086#post892086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm okay with a shapeshifter using size altering powers in creative ways but the 2mm tall Dawn Caste crushing everything in their path seems really, really dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of an earlier discussion in which a presumably-Full-Moon Lunar cartoonishly snapped the neck of a Dragon-Blooded as a common housefly. I was... against that.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, definitely in agreement that 1-5 doesn't really fit anymore when you can weigh less than a flicked booger. Excepting some factor giving you Ant-Man's disproportionate strength, potent venom, et cetera., a character being the size of a small insect should be really, <i>really</i> limited in his ability to harm a human-sized combatant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:18:11-07:00","id":892097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892086#post892086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm anti ant-sized humans because the 1-5 scale fails miserably to do it justice and in this game, human normally = Exaltation.<br /> I'm okay with a shapeshifter using size altering powers in creative ways but the 2mm tall Dawn Caste crushing everything in their path seems really, really dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Objection!<br /> <br /> 30.3mm is the minimum size for a Tiny Dawn, because that's one Japanese <i>sun</i>. Thus, Issun Boshi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:19:07-07:00","id":892098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892097#post892097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objection!<br /> <br /> 30.3mm is the minimum size for a Tiny Dawn, because that's one Japanese <i>sun</i>. Thus, Issun Boshi.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, roughly the size of a Space Marine miniature. I find that hysterical and damaging to my sense of drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T18:02:01-07:00","id":892158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891983#post891983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting with literally the entire Underworld, which is in fact irrelevant by design in the setting history until it becomes relevant for a setting event (ie, the Deathlord offensive starting).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich people love so much that they periodically start threads asking how to fix the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many things even are there in the setting that, when stripped from the frills, basically read &quot;these things were created because of nonsense reason X, and now are there waiting in case your players want to interact with them&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Enough to dissatisfy me to the extent that I can articulate my general standards for what should and shouldn't be in the setting.<br /> <br /> I find the argument of &quot;you can't dispute an addition on X grounds when X is already in some parts of the setting&quot; to be approaching from the wrong direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You have entire species of beasts literally created to do nothing but putz around inside tombs for millenia to guard them (Compass South, I seem to remember?) because they're there because they could be an interesting thing for the PCs to encounter. You have entire spirit genera with no other use than being a thing what sleeps under the earth for your players to encounter if they go delving.</div> </div> </div> </div> Things that aren't sapient don't quite entail the same necessities.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's a limit; there's a point at which something that exists solely to do some of that is just dull, but that's still apart from the point of whether they contribute to a richly engaging setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Heck, a lot of Masters of Jade was barely disguised weird plot hooks and interesting little oddities for players to latch on.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given that Masters of Jade is my gold standard of how to write a setting, I find your read to be mistaken.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:03:41-07:00","id":892851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=891982#post891982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to throw an observation into here that unifies how Lunar shapeshifting works, I'd say they take the forms of others with the emphasis being on &quot;take.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with this reasoning is that under this logic, it seems really strange that the spirit shape and Deadly Beastman Transformation are core, iconic Lunar abilities. They've always had a broad selection of shapeshifting powers that didn't involve taking others' forms, but those were non-core powers so they could stay or go. However, the spirit shape and DBT are actually probably more fundamental to the Lunar concept than stealing shapes from others, which seems incompatible with the notion that Lunar shifting is fundamentally about form-stealing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:12:11-07:00","id":892855,"title":"","content":"Little people don't interact well with Exalted's 1-5 dot rated traits or the combat system which uses those traits, and entire societies of little people working to build your clocks will get EXACTLY as much mechanical rules-support as a normal city's ability to build your fleet of sail boats.<br /> <br /> Societies of little people are also much easier to accidentally kill. One house fire that kills a human family would destroy a metropolis of little people. Little people would also find it harder to migrate across Creation, which means that fewer environmental disasters are needed to make them extinct.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Lunar ability to grow large or small, consider how far 3rd Edition is stepping away from the escalation and post-Essence 5 power levels of Second Edition, and ask yourself what would be the REASONABLE limits for how much bigger a Lunar could make any of their forms. Especially when turning into Godzilla can easily be left in the province of &quot;killing and drinking Godzilla&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's only so big or little a given form can become before it falls outside of the scale at which it actually WORKS, and the Lunar Exalted of all people are best equipped to assume forms which are actually DESIGNED to operate at any given scale without needing to resort to growing or shrinking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:08:44-07:00","id":894071,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm back! Very interesting points discussed here.<br /> <br /> I haven't read 2nd ed lunars in years, but I think I remember a knack to asume giant totem form... I don't mean being able to take a big animal as totem, but rather become a giant version of your totem (ginormous hummingbird terrorizing the Realm, etc)... I think it was in DotFA? Am I right?<br /> <br /> Also, I think Glories Luna had a knack to become a swarm... but I'm not completely sure. You can get inside a Warstrider as a swarm of spiders and kill the pilot in close quarters combat. Although I'm not sure how the system could handle that. However, I think those might be some ways in which lunars can show some interesting size changing magics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:49:30-07:00","id":894113,"title":"","content":"I don't think a Lunar should be able to make their spirit shape larger than a Solar can make their familiar.<br /> <br /> Of course, if a Lunar can make their spirit shape larger, why not their human form? Explanations are possible, but there are more lame ones than good ones, so care has to be taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:53:45-07:00","id":894119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894113#post894113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a Lunar should be able to make their spirit shape larger than a Solar can make their familiar.<br /> <br /> Of course, if a Lunar can make their spirit shape larger, why not their human form? Explanations are possible, but there are more lame ones than good ones, so care has to be taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are good explanations for making their human forms larger? Like, any, at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:01:22-07:00","id":894172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892855#post892855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Societies of little people are also much easier to accidentally kill. One house fire that kills a human family would destroy a metropolis of little people. Little people would also find it harder to migrate across Creation, which means that fewer environmental disasters are needed to make them extinct.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes, that image was part of what precipitated my whole question of how they fit in. I'm just imagining something like Smurf Village, where it takes one honey badger attack to just lick it up entirely. Something that would resemble a human society is not really adapted to exist at that scale. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:10:21-07:00","id":894267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894172#post894172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYes, that image was part of what precipitated my whole question of how they fit in. I'm just imagining something like Smurf Village, where it takes one honey badger attack to just lick it up entirely. Something that would resemble a human society is not really adapted to exist at that scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even just rats and squirrels. Ticks, lice and mosquitoes would be terrifying at that scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:34:09-07:00","id":894283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892855#post892855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only so big or little a given form can become before it falls outside of the scale at which it actually WORKS, and the Lunar Exalted of all people are best equipped to assume forms which are actually DESIGNED to operate at any given scale without needing to resort to growing or shrinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>That line inspired a swarm of thoughts going of into various directions in my head, some of them ending in questions. But basically, I agree.<br /> <br /> Now, excuse me while I rant and try to get back from one of those questions to the &quot;Lunars don't become big, they turn into things that already are big&quot;-statement...<br /> Can an escape artist Solar fit through a hole that's smaller than his head? There should be no way for this to be possible, but given that stealth Solars can literally hide in someone's shadow and gets pretty close to teleporting from shadow to shadow, &quot;impossibly tiny holes&quot; shouldn't be impossible. Similarily, a stealth solar can seem tiny and insignificant when he's actually a six-and-a-half foot tall athlete, and a war/presence/brawl solar can, independently of his actual size, walk across a battlefield with the presence of a giant and wrestle gozilla to the ground.<br /> <br /> None of this <i>actually</i> makes them bigger or smaller, but if &quot;themselves, but bigger&quot; or &quot;themselves, but smaller&quot; was a thing, then to me it would seem more fitting for a solar than a lunar, because &quot;flat out general amplification&quot; seems more solar-y to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now excuse me while I hide from those outraged by the idea that something that used to be a lunar thing might actually be better as a solar thing. If the mask ends up broken, you won't know it was me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:02:27-07:00","id":894303,"title":"","content":"I think shrinking and growing is inherent to the &quot;consummate shapeshifter&quot; motif and powerset. If you have a full-fledged protean archetype, it should be something they can do.<br /> <br /> Is there a full-fledged protean archetype in Exalted? Should there be? If there is, is it something other than a Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:40:45-07:00","id":894329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894119#post894119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are good explanations for making their human forms larger? Like, any, at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The construction of my sentence was intended to convey &quot;good explanations for why they can make their animal form bigger, but not their human form&quot;.<br /> <br /> To turn the question on its head, WHY can Lunars make their spirit shapes (or any animal forms) larger? If they can't do it for their birth forms or stolen human forms, why animals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:23:46-07:00","id":894359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894329#post894329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The construction of my sentence was intended to convey &quot;good explanations for why they can make their animal form bigger, but not their human form&quot;.<br /> <br /> To turn the question on its head, WHY can Lunars make their spirit shapes (or any animal forms) larger? If they can't do it for their birth forms or stolen human forms, why animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>How much bigger are we talking, anyway? If we get the Super Swole Strength Charm that had a boring, reused name in 1e, would that be big enough? Its principle cause would be to increase Strength in any form, but it might give some people what they're looking for.<br /> <br /> Most human forms, though, seem to be taken for the sake of deception and blending in with crowds. Going in with EOE wouldn't really fit, since it would rapidly get into the same territory as Ant-Man, only in reverse, and would rather lack the spark that Lunars have when turning their totem beast form into totemic kaijuu forms. At that point, it would be too much Ultraman, not enough Gamera or Godzilla.<br /> <br /> (Now recalling GURPS Monsters and its King Kong expy, along with the Godzilla-alike and a reference to a &quot;Mile High Guy&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:29:01-07:00","id":894364,"title":"","content":"For me... it goes back to Charms/Knacks being &quot;tools&quot; rather than &quot;tricks.&quot; They're something you have the capacity to do, and then apply in various ways.<br /> <br /> If you have the &quot;turn into a giant mouse&quot; Charm, that's a trick. It does one thing.<br /> <br /> If you have the &quot;turn into a mouse&quot; Charm and the &quot;turn giant&quot; Charm, though, that's a combination of tools that happen to let you become a giant mouse...but also let you do a number of other things. Like become a giant mosquito, or a giant T-Rex, or a giant human, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:02:03-07:00","id":894470,"title":"","content":"Becoming bigger is pretty key to the whole &quot;mythological monster&quot; thing. Lunars like Leviathan are supposed to be able to emulate mythological creatures like the leviathan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:21:11-07:00","id":894476,"title":"","content":"Every time I see this thread, I think it's about someone asking if it was safe to put their Lunar in the wash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:30:48-07:00","id":894481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894359#post894359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we get the Super Swole Strength Charm that had a boring, reused name in 1e, would that be big enough? Its principle cause would be to increase Strength in any form, but it might give some people what they're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine by me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much bigger are we talking, anyway? </div> </div> </div>Iunno.<br /> <br /> Using Solar familiars as a metric, the current limit with printed Charms is an optional permanent size increase of 50%, with a total temporary size increase of 140%.<br /> <br /> [y * 10%] (Life of the Aurochs) + 25% (Saga Beast Virtue) + 15% (Deadly Predator Method) + [y * 10%] (Deadly Predator Method), where &quot;y&quot; = number of times you purchased Life of the Aurochs.<br /> <br /> There may be some confused editing with regards to the interaction of Deadly Predator Method and Life of the Aurochs; it may only be intended to be counted once rather than twice. In which case, the maximum temporary size increase is 90%. Which is just barely <i>doubling </i>the familiar's size.<br /> <br /> I think Lunars can safely double the size of any form they can take without straying outside of their aesthetic themes, especially since that's just about perfect for &quot;clearly gain advantages in might and toughness without becoming so much larger that you need to adjust how the form interacts with the game's basic systems.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most human forms, though, seem to be taken for the sake of deception and blending in with crowds. </div> </div> </div>That's not a reason for Lunars to lack the option; it's just a reason why most Lunars won't ever bother USING the option. You don't need to outlaw revolvers when everyone wants to use automatics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894470#post894470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming bigger is pretty key to the whole &quot;mythological monster&quot; thing. Lunars like Leviathan are supposed to be able to emulate mythological creatures like the leviathan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Form lock is dead. You don't need to use your &quot;true forms&quot; for EVERYTHING now. You can freely use stolen forms, even when those stolen forms are much larger than your original ones.<br /> <br /> If Leviathan doesn't think being a twice-as-large-as-normal killer whale is enough, he can turn into a sea serpent he ate once.<br /> <br /> Or he can use Sorcery. Or artifacts. Or divine blessings. Or Wyld Mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:38:08-07:00","id":894483,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm just being dense, but I honestly don't know what point you're trying to make here.<br /> <br /> Are you trying to reconcile Lunar big-ness with that silly &quot;it's all about form-stealing&quot; thing SLS posted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T18:38:12-07:00","id":894484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894283#post894283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can an escape artist Solar fit through a hole that's smaller than his head?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by shrinking his head, he doesn't.<br /> <br /> Instead, he uses Lock-Opening Touch to just open the entire door. Or else he phases through the entire door with Door-Evading Technique.<br /> <br /> Based on those examples, and your own example of Shadow Replacement Technique, if a Solar ever develops a &quot;slip out of binding ropes&quot; Charm or a &quot;slip through the cracks in the walls&quot; Charm, it will probably work by the Solar simply phasing through it, teleporting around it, or turning into a living shadow or beam of light to slip through.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:39:12-07:00","id":894509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894484#post894484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not by shrinking his head, he doesn't.<br /> <br /> Instead, he uses Lock-Opening Touch to just open the entire door. Or else he phases through the entire door with Door-Evading Technique.<br /> <br /> Based on those examples, and your own example of Shadow Replacement Technique, if a Solar ever develops a &quot;slip out of binding ropes&quot; Charm or a &quot;slip through the cracks in the walls&quot; Charm, it will probably work by the Solar simply phasing through it, teleporting around it, or turning into a living shadow or beam of light to slip through.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Slipping into a shadow or turning into light seems a far step away from where Solars are trying to be taken (and where they kinda always wanted to be) of normals dudes trying really hard and doing impossible things. I can see a Solar Larceny Bro wriggling through a super tiny crack or opening a door without actually opening the door, but transfiguration and that jazz seems to be better left to Lunars and Sorcery. Of course, Solars can also cause the Apocalypse because they are smart in this edition so so much for that imagery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:54:50-07:00","id":894517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894483#post894483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm just being dense, but I honestly don't know what point you're trying to make here.<br /> <br /> Are you trying to reconcile Lunar big-ness with that silly &quot;it's all about form-stealing&quot; thing SLS posted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because trying to keep in line with the skinwalker and werebeast inspirations is totally silly.<br /> <br /> You want a huge human form without the ties to concepts that Lunars use? Go with Infernals or one of the other Exalted types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:08:45-07:00","id":894520,"title":"","content":"I think you may have misread my post, because your rebuttal doesn't actually contradict me.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Okay, I should probably explain a bit. SLS's explanation of Lunar shapeshifting is silly because it doesn't actually fit the way Lunars have been written. It doesn't even allow for Deadly Beastman Transformation, the most iconic Lunar shapeshifting power of all.<br /> <br /> And while I have no problem with Lunars growing huge in human form, I'm not actually arguing that they should be able to here. They have to be able to grow huge somehow, that's all I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:32:07-07:00","id":894534,"title":"","content":"Towering Beast Form -- the Lunar can assume the forms of beasts larger than a moose, if he has the Heart's Blood for them<br /> <br /> Emperor Ox Expansion -- the Lunar's frame swells and fills with excessive amounts of muscle mass; his form becomes twice as large, with bonuses to Strength<br /> <br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression -- the Lunar's war form grows as large as his spirit shape; this is possibly a DBT-derived Evocation of sorts, intended for Lunars whose spirit shapes are those of elephants and lizard lizards.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I am huge! That means I have huge guts! RIP AND TEAR!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T02:56:22-07:00","id":894637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894520#post894520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it doesn't actually fit the way Lunars have been written.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably going to be able to be said of a lot of what we get out of Lunars from herein.<br /> <br /> \u200bGiven the complaints of the past, it seems a reasonable pursuit, however it ultimately turns out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't even allow for Deadly Beastman Transformation, the most iconic Lunar shapeshifting power of all.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are a few things going on there. The first is how Lea's opening statement is about taking alternate forms; the war form is an elaboration on the one shape a Lunar never happens to take.<br /> <br /> The other is that he does suggest a connection between forms that have been stolen and extending those forms to mythic proportions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:23:15-07:00","id":894760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894476#post894476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time I see this thread, I think it's about someone asking if it was safe to put their Lunar in the wash.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is &quot;no.&quot; The Lunar will likely take exception.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I still think we need to analyze the broader question of whether Exalted has or should have a fully protean shifter-type. And, if so, whether Lunars should be that type. And, of not Lunars, then who?<br /> <br /> I contend that a fully protean shifter-type should have size-changing abilities.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, this argument boils down to the first consideration I listed above: are Lunars the fully-protean masters of shapeshifting or not? And, if not, who is? Raksha? Gods? Elementals? Luna alone? Infernals?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:41:02-07:00","id":894768,"title":"","content":"Oh, here's an image.<br /> <br /> Lunar size-growing ought to make a man-sized form &quot;Dark Souls humanoid-boss&quot; big. Big enough to be noticeable, powerful, intimidating, but not so big that the scale or scope of the fight changes.<br /> <br /> Big like Gwyn or Ornstein, but not like the Dancer of the Boreal Valley or the Stray Demon, who can both pick you up one-handed. Not big like the Stray Demon or Old Demon King, whom struggle to hit you if you can stay in their blind spots stabbing them in the ass.<br /> <br /> This is all speaking strictly about using man-sized forms for fighting men-sized opponents, of course. But a tyrant lizard fighting another tyrant who is twice her mass is in for a rough fight while not actually requiring completely different tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-20-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:45:31-07:00","id":894772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892095#post892095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reminded of an earlier discussion in which a presumably-Full-Moon Lunar cartoonishly snapped the neck of a Dragon-Blooded as a common housefly. I was... against that.</div> </div> </div> </div> I keep laughing at my mental image of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=892095#post892095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, definitely in agreement that 1-5 doesn't really fit anymore when you can weigh less than a flicked booger. Excepting some factor giving you Ant-Man's disproportionate strength, potent venom, et cetera., a character being the size of a small insect should be really, <i>really</i> limited in his ability to harm a human-sized combatant.</div> </div> </div> </div>For an insect form I'd go with Subtle/Poisonable tags on most of their attacks and maybe some kind of Latent ability gambit for attacking the target from the inside. The Tiny Creature merit would still be adequate for something so small; it\u2019s just that their definition of \u2018larger foe\u2019 would include things that also had it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:02:10-07:00","id":894785,"title":"","content":"The book had something like poisoned throwing darts, didn't it? Where the attack itself can't actually deal any damage, but is an effective vector for poisoning?<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, for a Lunar who takes the form of an insect... I would not care for neck-snapping, but surgical burrowing is a horse of a different colour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:19:12-07:00","id":894798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894760#post894760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is &quot;no.&quot; The Lunar will likely take exception.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I still think we need to analyze the broader question of whether Exalted has or should have a fully protean shifter-type. And, if so, whether Lunars should be that type. And, of not Lunars, then who?<br /> <br /> I contend that a fully protean shifter-type should have size-changing abilities.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, this argument boils down to the first consideration I listed above: are Lunars the fully-protean masters of shapeshifting or not? And, if not, who is? Raksha? Gods? Elementals? Luna alone? Infernals?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you're just going to aimlessly ask without any structural concept in mind, probably no one. &quot;Fully protean&quot; in this case seems to be an unfettered application of Aberrant's Shapeshifting power, which could change a character into just about anything. That needs to get nailed down for just about any concept intended to interact with Exalted. And the nailing down usually needs to be rather extensive, because it is such a wide-open power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:31:38-07:00","id":894805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894798#post894798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're just going to aimlessly ask without any structural concept in mind, probably no one. &quot;Fully protean&quot; in this case seems to be an unfettered application of Aberrant's Shapeshifting power, which could change a character into just about anything. That needs to get nailed down for just about any concept intended to interact with Exalted. And the nailing down usually needs to be rather extensive, because it is such a wide-open power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I should have said, &quot;Is there any order of being which has the potential to become a fully protean shapeshifter?&quot; I don't mean this as a &quot;buy this power and you're fully protean&quot; sort of deal. I meant this as a question of whether this falls within anybody's bailiwick. It could be that your answer is, &quot;No. Under no circumstances should any character be that flexible in its shapeshifting prowess in Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> If so, however, I question &quot;why not?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:40:43-07:00","id":894810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894805#post894805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps I should have said, &quot;Is there any order of being which has the potential to become a fully protean shapeshifter?&quot; I don't mean this as a &quot;buy this power and you're fully protean&quot; sort of deal. I meant this as a question of whether this falls within anybody's bailiwick. It could be that your answer is, &quot;No. Under no circumstances should any character be that flexible in its shapeshifting prowess in Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> If so, however, I question &quot;why not?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What theme are you looking for? NB: &quot;Fully protean shapeshifter&quot; is not a theme. Even Proteus turned into normal examples of beasts, water, and plant life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:55:42-07:00","id":894828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894810#post894810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What theme are you looking for? NB: &quot;Fully protean shapeshifter&quot; is not a theme. Even Proteus turned into normal examples of beasts, water, and plant life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say Morph from the X-Men comics, or Odo from Deep Space Nine, or any of the shape-shifters from more modern mythology (TV, books, comics, etc.) that can kind of turn into anything. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:10:13-07:00","id":894833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894828#post894828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's say Morph from the X-Men comics, or Odo from Deep Space Nine, or any of the shape-shifters from more modern mythology (TV, books, comics, etc.) that can kind of turn into anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the exact wording I said wasn't a theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:15:43-07:00","id":894836,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Odo from DS9&quot; definitely had a theme.<br /> <br /> I didn't say it's sufficient to hang a whole splat on, by itself. I said that there should be something with that theme. Not that that theme should be the entirety of a splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:16:13-07:00","id":894837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894833#post894833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty much the exact wording I said wasn't a theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my examples were meant to illustrate that it IS a theme, and has been used as such in multiple places throughout the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:45:23-07:00","id":894856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894805#post894805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps I should have said, &quot;Is there any order of being which has the potential to become a fully protean shapeshifter?&quot; I don't mean this as a &quot;buy this power and you're fully protean&quot; sort of deal. I meant this as a question of whether this falls within anybody's bailiwick. It could be that your answer is, &quot;No. Under no circumstances should any character be that flexible in its shapeshifting prowess in Exalted.&quot;<br /> <br /> If so, however, I question &quot;why not?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it should be specifically excluded or anything, but I think the starting premise of &quot;<i>somebody</i> should have a perfect shapeshifting&quot; is not really necessary, and that starting off with that as a concept and working backwards to find or make somebody to assign it to is inorganic.<br /> <br /> I mean, Lucien has always been described as a particularly excellent shapeshifter, but I doubt Jenna Moran started with the idea of shapeshifting demon and worked back to the whole hunter of rebels thing. Conversely, his shapeshifting is an organic quality for Lucien, but I doubt it's the first thing people remember about him.<br /> <br /> I think Exalted is generally focused on characters whose powers and imagery are complex and intricate enough that things based on straightforward, singular powers (even if they're broad in scope) are not entirely fitting amongst them. Not quite a case of &quot;shouldn't be in the setting&quot; as not exactly in the same arena as Exalted and spirits.<br /> <br /> To me, it sounds a bit like the kind of thing that a powerful sorcerous working could make; that line under the Solar workings of making something powerful of a &quot;unitary nature&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Which, incidentally, is the wording I focus on to articulate why sorcery does not make Exalted, if ever it should come up again)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:48:25-07:00","id":894915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894837#post894837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, my examples were meant to illustrate that it IS a theme, and has been used as such in multiple places throughout the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a theme, it's a generic power suite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:08:40-07:00","id":894933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=894915#post894915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a theme, it's a generic power suite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like we'll be disagreeing on this point, then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:16:48-07:00","id":894940,"title":"","content":"It's like saying being a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FlyingBrick\" target=\"_blank\">Flying Brick</a> is a theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:41:20-07:00","id":894958,"title":"","content":"I miss that Rick and Morty clip. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:33:19-07:00","id":895006,"title":"","content":"So, then, is &quot;human excellence&quot; a theme, or a power suite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:40:29-07:00","id":895015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=895006#post895006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then, is &quot;human excellence&quot; a theme, or a power suite?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's barely even a descriptor, to be honest, much less a power suite or a theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:41:09-07:00","id":895016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=895006#post895006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then, is &quot;human excellence&quot; a theme, or a power suite?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, if we're talking ludicrous levels of it. Luckily, Solars have themes that support them in having said power suite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T15:47:07-07:00","id":895057,"title":"","content":"Yes, human excellence is a theme of the Solars, it being an idea that recurs in and pervades their narrative and imagery. Same as any other mythology that makes a point of having exemplary human champions discover secrets, conquer nature, or destroy monsters that stand as an obstacle to humanity. Human excellence is a theme of the mythology of Heracles, for instance.<br /> <br /> It is a theme to Solar powers insofar as it is the purpose to which their powers are directed, and that guides and constrains their cosmetics.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shapeshifting&quot; was not Odo's theme; alienation even by the standards of a world of such diversity of the Star Trek universe was. That Odo's true form was a shapeshifting fluid was in service of that theme; that Odo's default appearance is a crude attempt to emulate the people around him was in service to that theme, both in terms of his desire to try and fit in, and how in spite of that there's still an indelible bar between him and them.<br /> <br /> The Lunars will have a theme; they should have shapeshifting guided within the confines of serving it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:22:52-07:00","id":896786,"title":"","content":"So, then, Lunars do not have &quot;shapeshifting&quot; as a theme, since it is not a theme?<br /> <br /> Does this mean that we should not be responding to somebody asking, &quot;How do I play a shapeshifter?&quot; by saying &quot;Play a Lunar?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:26:25-07:00","id":896794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=896786#post896786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then, Lunars do not have &quot;shapeshifting&quot; as a theme, since it is not a theme?<br /> <br /> Does this mean that we should not be responding to somebody asking, &quot;How do I play a shapeshifter?&quot; by saying &quot;Play a Lunar?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, said individual is asking a pretty vague question about who has a set of ill-defined powers, not anything else. You'd have to find out what, exactly, they were looking for in shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> But yes, to answer your question, the theme of the Lunars isn't shapeshifting. It's being a dual-natured, somewhat monstrous hero with shades of being a warrior, trickster, and shaman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:39:54-07:00","id":896805,"title":"","content":"&quot;Shapeshifter&quot; is an almost uselessly broad descriptor. When you say shapeshifter, do you mean like a werewolf, like Mystique, like Mr. Fantastic, like Ant-Man, like Ms. Marvel, like Alex Mercer, like Apocalypse, like Beast Boy, like Ulquiorra Cifer, or like the Thing (John Carpenter version, not the orange rock guy)? Because those are all extremely different ideas and if you don't have your parameters for <i>what kind of shapeshifter</i> you are working with established at the outset, you're going to have a mess on your hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:50:19-07:00","id":896809,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OurMonstersAreDifferent\" target=\"_blank\">Sorta like demons, dragons, and vampires, but even <i>less</i> coherent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:06:47-07:00","id":896896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=896809#post896809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OurMonstersAreDifferent\" target=\"_blank\">Sorta like demons, dragons, and vampires, but even <i>less</i> coherent. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a></div> </div> </div> </div>But...<sub>those are all bases for Exalted archetypes...</sub>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:43:49-07:00","id":896938,"title":"","content":"I do find it interesting how some of the people in this conversation argued exactly the opposite positions a few years ago. I will assume it represents a shift in what they believe the Lunar paradigm should be in 3E vs. what it was in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:46:40-07:00","id":897026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=896896#post896896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But...<sub>those are all bases for Exalted archetypes...</sub></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they picked out specific versions of them and defined their limits when they used those mythic archetypes to create various kinds of Exalted. The Dragon Blooded are based out of various Asian dragon myths, not the western fire breathing, damsel snatching, and gold hording types.<br /> <br /> ....Though, given the way the Realm works, I could see some arguments to be made about that, I suppose.<br /> <br /> The point is that, if you pick any broad archetype, like Shapeshifter, as your design basis, you need to define it further, otherwise you'll end up with a conflicting mess of tropes and complications on your hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T12:52:13-07:00","id":897085,"title":"","content":"Lunars consume other things and take their nature in to them, and become those things that they consume. You can't turn in to anything you haven't consumed. This is a pretty strict constraint! But as they increase in power, I would assume that the possible values of 'thing' and possible meanings of 'consume' can all become less literal.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, one of the more memorable scenes I've STd in Exalted was a fight between a Lunar in the form of a mosquito and a Stomach Bottle Bug being waged in the esophagus of the Guild factor the lunar sought to assassinate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T12:55:33-07:00","id":897088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=896938#post896938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do find it interesting how some of the people in this conversation argued exactly the opposite positions a few years ago. I will assume it represents a shift in what they believe the Lunar paradigm should be in 3E vs. what it was in 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguing with certain parties in the time between the final Scroll of Errata update and the announcement of EX3 made me realize an awful lot. One of those things was &quot;don't ditch the seed of W:tA from the Lunars&quot;. If you do, you end up with total incoherence, and people will try to come up with all manner of ways to patch the yawning void you've left. Nothing really cuts it like the original, though. <br /> <br /> So, now, if people start railing against the werewolf-ness of Lunars, &quot;Before My Body is Dry&quot; plays in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:30:33-07:00","id":897117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897088#post897088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arguing with certain parties in the time between the final Scroll of Errata update and the announcement of EX3 made me realize an awful lot. One of those things was &quot;don't ditch the seed of W:tA from the Lunars&quot;. If you do, you end up with total incoherence, and people will try to come up with all manner of ways to patch the yawning void you've left. Nothing really cuts it like the original, though.<br /> <br /> So, now, if people start railing against the werewolf-ness of Lunars, &quot;Before My Body is Dry&quot; plays in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I disagree. I greatly dislike W;tA and I dislike it's influence. Now I've more or less accepted that Ex3 Lunars will probably go back to a lot of the W:tA inspiration, but I feel it's honestly deeply insincere to try to argue that W:tA inspiration is the ONLY coherent inspiration for Lunars. It might be the vision you support and perhaps it will be the vision Ex3 goes with, but other visions exist and they aren't automatically 'incoherent' just because they ditched the W;tA elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:45:21-07:00","id":897133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897117#post897117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I disagree. I greatly dislike W;tA and I dislike it's influence. Now I've more or less accepted that Ex3 Lunars will probably go back to a lot of the W:tA inspiration, but I feel it's honestly deeply insincere to try to argue that W:tA inspiration is the ONLY coherent inspiration for Lunars. It might be the vision you support and perhaps it will be the vision Ex3 goes with, but other visions exist and they aren't automatically 'incoherent' just because they ditched the W;tA elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the bedrock to ground what kind of shapeshifting they use. I imagine that they'll go to a lot of other places in other arenas, notably because there are no issues of bloodlines (that's the Dragon-Blooded's thing) or messing up the world through alienation of your allies (the Sidereals!)., but the shapeshifting is going to seem somewhat familiar, as will their approximate role in the world (beaten down but still fighting on against large institutions to determine the shape of what follows after the present world falls). This follows from the 1e STC's explanation that Exalted isn't really the prehistory of the WoD, it's just a setting with a lot of similar details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:50:17-07:00","id":897139,"title":"","content":"Personally - and I apologize if I was being coy earlier, but I was trying to tease out positions and concerns without polluting it too much with my own viewpoint - I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> is largely correct regarding the seed and starting point. However, while I don't think &quot;total protean shapeshifter&quot; is the be-all and end-all of Lunars, I do think it is something <b>a</b> Lunar should be able to do, if he wants to go that way as <b>his</b> expression of his magics. Another Lunar, perhaps, should be able to focus on other things, even limiting himself to &quot;being Mystique&quot; in his shifting, because he has other extensions of the core starting point he's pursuing.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of where the themes and powers CAN go, not where they MUST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:57:27-07:00","id":897152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897139#post897139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally - and I apologize if I was being coy earlier, but I was trying to tease out positions and concerns without polluting it too much with my own viewpoint - I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> is largely correct regarding the seed and starting point. However, while I don't think &quot;total protean shapeshifter&quot; is the be-all and end-all of Lunars, I do think it is something <b>a</b> Lunar should be able to do, if he wants to go that way as <b>his</b> expression of his magics. Another Lunar, perhaps, should be able to focus on other things, even limiting himself to &quot;being Mystique&quot; in his shifting, because he has other extensions of the core starting point he's pursuing.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of where the themes and powers CAN go, not where they MUST.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just described second edition Lunars. All of those &quot;options&quot; are just diluting them in said edition, because any shapeshifting outside of the arena of humans and animals is not for the Lunars - but, thanks to the capabilities of beasts and various spiritual and intuitive primal facilities that also anchor Lunars in EX3, that's probably not going to put them behind anyone. Quite the contrary, in fact..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:59:22-07:00","id":897156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897117#post897117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I disagree. I greatly dislike W;tA and I dislike it's influence. Now I've more or less accepted that Ex3 Lunars will probably go back to a lot of the W:tA inspiration, but I feel it's honestly deeply insincere to try to argue that W:tA inspiration is the ONLY coherent inspiration for Lunars. It might be the vision you support and perhaps it will be the vision Ex3 goes with, but other visions exist and they aren't automatically 'incoherent' just because they ditched the W;tA elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. I mean, to be honest, for me the &quot;famous&quot; parts of World of Darkness are among the least interest-grabbing RP settings to ever attain commercial success (and this is competing with freaking Greyhawk, so that's a feat), so I am most likely biased, but I am kind of very much not enthusiastic about &quot;going back to WtA roots&quot;. <br /> <br /> I know it's what's going to happen. I'm not trying to convince anyone it's not. I just don't have to like it, in the same way I never, from moment zero, liked Infernals, when the forum was raving about them. So I'm going to grumble a lot and in the unlikely case I ever ST Ex3 and any of my players ever wants to play a Lunar just add a pile of stuff beyond the &quot;predatory therianthrope&quot; standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:29:25-07:00","id":897189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897152#post897152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just described second edition Lunars. All of those &quot;options&quot; are just diluting them in said edition, because any shapeshifting outside of the arena of humans and animals is not for the Lunars - but, thanks to the capabilities of beasts and various spiritual and intuitive primal facilities that also anchor Lunars in EX3, that's probably not going to put them behind anyone. Quite the contrary, in fact..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are conflating things that were problems in overall writing with unrelated developments. Lunars didn't suffer dilution because of such things; they suffered dilution because they started as &quot;Silver Solars&quot; and had no basis for growth. I was one of those arguing FOR the animal-base and otherness as core starting points. I just happen to think they can branch from there. Not all Lunars must or should. That's the point of having a solid core. But moving out from that core in various directions is what one does as one specializes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:37:25-07:00","id":897201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897189#post897189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are conflating things that were problems in overall writing with unrelated developments. Lunars didn't suffer dilution because of such things; they suffered dilution because they started as &quot;Silver Solars&quot; and had no basis for growth. I was one of those arguing FOR the animal-base and otherness as core starting points. I just happen to think they can branch from there. Not all Lunars must or should. That's the point of having a solid core. But moving out from that core in various directions is what one does as one specializes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Silver Solar Charms and no strong concept to what shapeshifting was supposed to do made 2e Lunars tepid and boring, particularly when a number of even more loose &quot;options&quot; was given in its terrible brand of chimerism. There's no real call to couch it in terms of core and expansion; they have a central concept for it, and they don't expand infinitely in every direction as time goes on. No gods, no elementals, no demons, no ghosts. Just beasts and humanity, as Luna's preoccupation with Gaia had it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:57:39-07:00","id":897229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897088#post897088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arguing with certain parties in the time between the final Scroll of Errata update and the announcement of EX3 made me realize an awful lot. One of those things was &quot;don't ditch the seed of W:tA from the Lunars&quot;. If you do, you end up with total incoherence, and people will try to come up with all manner of ways to patch the yawning void you've left. Nothing really cuts it like the original, though.<br /> <br /> So, now, if people start railing against the werewolf-ness of Lunars, &quot;Before My Body is Dry&quot; plays in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1<br /> <br /> (ten count)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:58:40-07:00","id":897231,"title":"","content":"Eh. I disagree, then. I think it can and should expand beyond just beasts and humanity, if the Lunar in question wants to take it that way.<br /> <br /> I think that a strong root in the beasts themes will support such expansions. The dilution was due to lacking that strong foundation, not due to having the options exist at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T15:52:35-07:00","id":897278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897133#post897133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the bedrock to ground what kind of shapeshifting they use. I imagine that they'll go to a lot of other places in other arenas, notably because there are no issues of bloodlines (that's the Dragon-Blooded's thing) or messing up the world through alienation of your allies (the Sidereals!)., but the shapeshifting is going to seem somewhat familiar, as will their approximate role in the world (beaten down but still fighting on against large institutions to determine the shape of what follows after the present world falls). This follows from the 1e STC's explanation that Exalted isn't really the prehistory of the WoD, it's just a setting with a lot of similar details.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you describe is a possibility. it's a possibility that may end up being the canon one for Ex3 even. But it's not the ONLY valid path to take toward developing a coherent splat that is distinctly Lunar. You keep extolling the virtues of how this W:tA basis makes them so coherent, but it's really only a positive if you LIKE that basis. If you dislike it, it becomes a negative regardless of how coherent it is.<br /> <br /> The basic elements of their place in the setting is very 'simple' as of yet and not something W:tA has a monopoly on, nor is W:tA a particularly pure representative of such, it, itself having a number of other competing themes as well, by your own admission","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T16:53:28-07:00","id":897346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897278#post897278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you describe is a possibility. it's a possibility that may end up being the canon one for Ex3 even. But it's not the ONLY valid path to take toward developing a coherent splat that is distinctly Lunar. You keep extolling the virtues of how this W:tA basis makes them so coherent, but it's really only a positive if you LIKE that basis. If you dislike it, it becomes a negative regardless of how coherent it is.<br /> <br /> The basic elements of their place in the setting is very 'simple' as of yet and not something W:tA has a monopoly on, nor is W:tA a particularly pure representative of such, it, itself having a number of other competing themes as well, by your own admission</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, is it that the true source of your animosity that they aren't broad shapeshifters as you remember from 2e? Because 2e basically lied about what they were. It attached a superstructure to them that didn't fit. No one could apparently be bothered to jump above the low bar of 1e Lunars, they went around it, and it's only ended up causing more problems in the end.<br /> <br /> There's still no satisfactory reason to have one splat be every kind of shapeshifter. Even the WoD had the spread over multiple games, so maybe all of the other non-Solar splats will get some version of it. Abyssals can get their non-illusion mimicry back from 1e, Sidereals can do something involving vague mystical rules, and Dragon-Blooded might have something that looks like the capability of Clayface if you squint and filter it through wuxia films, but just because Lunars were one kind of shapeshifter in 1e is no real call to try and demolish the house to make it into a giant doorway with no walls..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:53:15-07:00","id":897497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897346#post897346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, is it that the true source of your animosity that they aren't broad shapeshifters as you remember from 2e? Because 2e basically lied about what they were. It attached a superstructure to them that didn't fit. No one could apparently be bothered to jump above the low bar of 1e Lunars, they went around it, and it's only ended up causing more problems in the end.<br /> <br /> There's still no satisfactory reason to have one splat be every kind of shapeshifter. Even the WoD had the spread over multiple games, so maybe all of the other non-Solar splats will get some version of it. Abyssals can get their non-illusion mimicry back from 1e, Sidereals can do something involving vague mystical rules, and Dragon-Blooded might have something that looks like the capability of Clayface if you squint and filter it through wuxia films, but just because Lunars were one kind of shapeshifter in 1e is no real call to try and demolish the house to make it into a giant doorway with no walls..</div> </div> </div> </div>...Uh, no, I'm pretty sure the source of my 'animosity' is I really dislike W:tA. Thanks(?) though.<br /> <br /> I think it's fair to say that Lunars should have a coherent thematic that encompasses their shapeshifting. I am asserting that W:tA isn't the only valid usable possibility for such. Moreover, you say 'non-Solar' but looking at Perfect Mirror+Persona charms I think it's safe to call that 'Solar Shapeshifting' after a style. Other splats having shapeshifting has never been the issue? I mean, there are a few 'splat niche' adherents, but Abyssals sewing/rearranging their face (in appropriate undead-ish horror inspired style) or DBs creating clay masks Clayface style or Sidereal's resplendent destinies they've always had.... none of that has ever really been an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T19:53:25-07:00","id":897498,"title":"","content":"Okay, now that's just plain silly. An edition can't lie about what a splat is. Whatever it says the splat is is what that splat is, at least for that edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897085#post897085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars consume other things and take their nature in to them, and become those things that they consume. You can't turn in to anything you haven't consumed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you can. See Deadly Beastman Transformation, Claws of the Silver Moon, Monkey Arm Style, Twin-Faced Hero, Changing Plumage Mastery, Flowing Body Evasion...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I maintain that even a broad interpretation of shapeshifting is not broader than human excellence, elemental themes, weird fate shenanigans, or machine powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:11:44-07:00","id":897510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897498#post897498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See Deadly Beastman Transformation</div> </div> </div> </div>A combination of the Lunar's birth form and spirit shape. The spirit shape is the exception that proves the rule by being the ONLY animal shape that the Lunar gets without Heart's Blood. The Lunar gets that shape because he is reborn as a Chosen of Luna; a semi-divine being with three souls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Claws of the Silver Moon </div> </div> </div>Didn't grow natural weapons; just enhanced the ones you have, whether those are human nails or cow horns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monkey Arm Style<br /> <br /> Flowing Body Evasion... </div> </div> </div>Liminal Charms.<br /> <br /> Lunars transform their bodies, holistically and spiritually assuming the shapes of beasts. Liminals are zombie-people who treat their bodies like playdough made of meat. Their muscles are bleeding clay, their tendons are leaking rubber bands, and their blood is ink with which they pen their legends.<br /> <br /> I believe that Armor-Forming Technique, where you grow bones over your body for protection, will be a Liminal trick rather than a Lunar one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Twin-Faced Hero, Changing Plumage Mastery </div> </div> </div>Shades of Luna? The moon is always the moon, but always with a different face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:24:05-07:00","id":897520,"title":"","content":"You could move that stuff from the Lunar wheelhouse to the Liminal one. But the Lunars we have, have that type of ability. And I'd like to see them keep it; it's an interesting and impressive type of power that is distinctly not Solar. Which really helps with the whole Silver Solar issue.<br /> <br /> The 2e description of Claws of the Silver Moon doesn't say anything about enhancing existing weapons. It gives you claws, whether you've got fingernails or not.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the totally-unrelated-to-form-theft shapeshifting is pretty direct Luna emulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T22:44:24-07:00","id":897588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897497#post897497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Uh, no, I'm pretty sure the source of my 'animosity' is I really dislike W:tA. Thanks(?) though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because you seem terribly invested in Lunars, which have been known to be derived from W:tA f<a href=\"https://youtu.be/l_A8yY_iyYk?t=270\" target=\"_blank\">or about 15 years, give or take</a>. They're probably not going to change on that, any more than Abyssals are likely to suddenly stop growing fangs and drinking blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's fair to say that Lunars should have a coherent thematic that encompasses their shapeshifting. </div> </div> </div>In light of every conversation about how damned broad shapeshifting is, why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am asserting that W:tA isn't the only valid usable possibility for such. </div> </div> </div>But why? What the hell has you so hellbent on scouring away the inspiration of a character type instead of waiting for other Exalted to come out and cover those bases?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, you say 'non-Solar' but looking at Perfect Mirror+Persona charms I think it's safe to call that 'Solar Shapeshifting' after a style. </div> </div> </div>Solars axiomatically do not shapeshift, per the description of their Charms. It's all magically-good acting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other splats having shapeshifting has never been the issue? I mean, there are a few 'splat niche' adherents, but Abyssals sewing/rearranging their face (in appropriate undead-ish horror inspired style) </div> </div> </div>They don't do that anymore; the grotesque stuff has gone to the Liminals. Abyssals are on the docket to be suave vampire-esque Exalted even more than before, and deal more with ghostly influences when they aren't doing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or DBs creating clay masks Clayface style or Sidereal's resplendent destinies they've always had.... none of that has ever really been an issue. </div> </div> </div>Then why are you arguing that Lunars need to be every type of shapeshifter? Other Exalted can cover the non-werewolfish bases.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T22:51:54-07:00","id":897591,"title":"","content":"As I said earlier, there's a huge gap between &quot;not really part of your central thing&quot; and &quot;not something you can do at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> eg. teleporting, flying, or dropping meteors on people are definitely not central to the Solar theme, but they're stuff you can reach from inside the Solar charmset if you approach them from the right angle and build up to them. (And conversely, while Solars have charms that can do all those things, you couldn't really build a Solar who does those as their primary shtick, not without building them very unintuitively or homebrewing a massive amount.)<br /> <br /> Some of the stuff people are requesting for Lunars is probably like that -- not a core thing, and not something you're likely to be able to build your entire Lunar around, but you could probably squeeze them in somewhere as a supplemental trick, especially if you can explain how you're building your way towards them out of their more central core themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T22:53:00-07:00","id":897592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897498#post897498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, now that's just plain silly. An edition can't lie about what a splat is. Whatever it says the splat is is what that splat is, at least for that edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's second edition. It was full of ideas that were, at best, misleading. I posit, thus, that it was entirely possible for it to give people the wrong impression about a character type; hell, it even did that in the first chapter of Infernals, on account of how the early chapter authors didn't know what the later chapter authors were doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, I maintain that even a broad interpretation of shapeshifting is not broader than human excellence, elemental themes, weird fate shenanigans, or machine powers. </div> </div> </div>Even if it were true (how many times do we have to go over just what untethered shapeshifting allows?), it wouldn't matter, because Lunars have never actually been limited solely to shapeshifting Charms. Scads of them in 1e were, admittedly while rather poorly written, cited something other than a change in form to accomplish what they did. Trances, visions, primordial knowledge of the flesh... we've been over this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T23:17:05-07:00","id":897601,"title":"","content":"Whether an impression is wrong or not is entirely determined by the edition itself, because it defines its own splats. Yes, sometimes an edition can be self-contradictory, but claiming that it presented a splat falsely as a whole is just plain silly.<br /> <br /> And while we have discussed the broadness of shapeshifting, we didn't agree that it's as broad as you imagine it to be. Mostly because it isn't.<br /> <br /> Trances, visions, flesh-knowledge, and were-wolf-ery are all narrow enough to coexist with untethered shapeshifting. Other possible Lunar themes aren't, so how broad their shapeshifting should be will have to depend on how their other themes are handled. But going all-in on the shapeshifting is an option, and I think it's a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T23:39:48-07:00","id":897611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Because you seem terribly invested in Lunars, which have been known to be derived from W:tA f<a href=\"https://youtu.be/l_A8yY_iyYk?t=270\" target=\"_blank\">or about 15 years, give or take</a>. They're probably not going to change on that, any more than Abyssals are likely to suddenly stop growing fangs and drinking blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting video where a Dev talks about how how the Exalt types are explicitly the predecessors to WoD splats. I think it's safe to say that some of what he is expressing there has sunk into irrelevance in Modern Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In light of every conversation about how damned broad shapeshifting is, why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't accept this as fact. It's also a disingenuous argument because it assumes doing the same thing over and over again using different 'types' of 'shapeshifting. I assume that when designing Lunars you would have them do certain things, certain ways to preserve thematic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why? What the hell has you so hellbent on scouring away the inspiration of a character type instead of waiting for other Exalted to come out and cover those bases?</div> </div> </div> </div>A) Did I mention I really mislike W:tA? Cause I really dislike it.<br /> B) Ex1 Lunars is widely considered one of the worst books in the franchise, on the same level as Scroll of the Monk or the first two chapters of Infernals. Ex2 Lunars stepped away from that and, when it was released, was actually quite beloved. It's overtime it's flaws have become apparent. It really feels like continuing the course away from Ex1 Lunars is the better path rather than racing back to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars axiomatically do not shapeshift, per the description of their Charms. It's all magically-good acting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Po-tay-toe, Po-tah-toe? You can say it isn't shapeshifting but you can enact such radical changes it's as much shapeshifting as many of the things you've already described as shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't do that anymore; the grotesque stuff has gone to the Liminals. Abyssals are on the docket to be suave vampire-esque Exalted even more than before, and deal more with ghostly influences when they aren't doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literially just repeated what you said back to you and you're disagreeing with me...? Whatever. As far as Abyssal not getting grotesque stuff? I'll beleive it when I see it, especially as the core says stuff like &quot;others embody the grave\u2019s decay, becoming drawn and withered, or even blooming into full and eternal rot.&quot; and &quot;ingenious war machines of bone and sinew.&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why are you arguing that Lunars need to be every type of shapeshifter? Other Exalted can cover the non-werewolfish bases.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep putting words in my mouth, it's a bit obnoxious. I never said I really wanted them to cover every type of shapeshifter, just not starting from a basis of W;tA. I should not that even THAT doesn't confine itself to just 'werewolf' shapeshifting, as they do more than just, you know, turn into a wolf or wolfman.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:07:03-07:00","id":897723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897588#post897588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Because you seem terribly invested in Lunars, which have been known to be derived from W:tA f<a href=\"https://youtu.be/l_A8yY_iyYk?t=270\" target=\"_blank\">or about 15 years, give or take</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amine Hsu's dislike isn't exactly unique.<br /> <br /> I remember a lot of people claim that trying to shove W:tA's Square Peg into Exalted's Round Hole was the reason Lunars were so unpopular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T08:14:47-07:00","id":897818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897346#post897346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because 2e basically lied about what they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call it more of a whitewash myself.<br /> <br /> The Lunars of 2e were unapologetic skinwalkers, since charms/knacks were distinct things so they actually called their ability to acquire human forms through murder Prey's Skin Disguise. Everything about the Thousand Streams River project is way darker once you realise that's going to be their default infiltration method.<br /> <br /> Not to mention controlling people from the shadows for the goal of ultimately liberating them from the Exalted has its own problems.<br /> Either Lunar influence is so effective that no mortal can resist it. The TSR is impossible.<br /> Or.<br /> There's mortals who can and do resist but then they're a loose end. The TSR is basically the worst aspects of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> It's a very similar flavour to &quot;The Scarlet Empire takes over and they'll protect you a lot better than you ever could&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:07:04-07:00","id":898008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897818#post897818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call it more of a whitewash myself.<br /> <br /> The Lunars of 2e were unapologetic skinwalkers, since charms/knacks were distinct things so they actually called their ability to acquire human forms through murder Prey's Skin Disguise. Everything about the Thousand Streams River project is way darker once you realise that's going to be their default infiltration method.<br /> <br /> Not to mention controlling people from the shadows for the goal of ultimately liberating them from the Exalted has its own problems.<br /> Either Lunar influence is so effective that no mortal can resist it. The TSR is impossible.<br /> Or.<br /> There's mortals who can and do resist but then they're a loose end. <b>The TSR is basically the worst aspects of Sidereals.</b><br /> <br /> It's a very similar flavour to &quot;The Scarlet Empire takes over and they'll protect you a lot better than you ever could&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I mean that's what concerns me the most about <i>Third Edition's</i> direction for Lunars - throwing hundreds-to-thousands of expendable dupes into pointless meat-grinder conflicts for purely-selfish reasons. At least Sidereals have the excuse of &quot;*mumblemumble* Destiny, *mumblemumble* greater good of all Creation,&quot; and - this is the crazy part - the books <i>never call them out on this</i>. Only for the Usurpation itself, and for their <i>failures </i>to act, as in the case of the Great Contagion; at no point is it ever seriously suggested that the Bureau of Destiny itself is the problem.<br /> <br /> I'll probably make a longer effortpost on this later, but a big part of the issue with W: tA as Lunar inspiration is that removing the Garou from the context of the World of Darkness also removes a lot of their justifications for existing. They don't fight to defend nature, because nature can defend itself just fine in Creation. They don't champion or defend the dispossessed, but instead sacrifice them in droves to buy a few more years for themselves. They don't represent any tribal societies or lineages because they're Celestial Exalted, set above and apart from the rest of their peoples, and the only marks of their heritage are beastfolk, born as living weapons for their forebears' sakes and basically as wronged by their progenitors as anyone they're sent to fight. Even when they do represent, defend, or otherwise give patronage to mortal societies, the devs themselves are on record that it's never made sense to <i>want </i>a Lunar in charge of anything - say (caveat: the devs have not said this, and it is purely my inference based on their statements), if someone in Perfect Soul's position were to be chosen by Luna instead of Sol, they would be <i>wrong </i>to do what she did; to kick out the occupiers and reassert themselves as the legitimate authority.<br /> <br /> Barring some major setting revelations to shake things up, 3e Lunars don't come across as Werewolf: the Apocalypse. They come across as Beast: the Primordial. <i>I have nothing nice to say about Beast.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:15:19-07:00","id":898068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898008#post898008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I mean that's what concerns me the most about <i>Third Edition's</i> direction for Lunars - throwing hundreds-to-thousands of expendable dupes into pointless meat-grinder conflicts for purely-selfish reasons. At least Sidereals have the excuse of &quot;*mumblemumble* Destiny, *mumblemumble* greater good of all Creation,&quot; and - this is the crazy part - the books <i>never call them out on this</i>. Only for the Usurpation itself, and for their <i>failures </i>to act, as in the case of the Great Contagion; at no point is it ever seriously suggested that the Bureau of Destiny itself is the problem.<br /> <br /> I'll probably make a longer effortpost on this later, but a big part of the issue with W: tA as Lunar inspiration is that removing the Garou from the context of the World of Darkness also removes a lot of their justifications for existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Luna loves Gaia and made her Exalted in Gaia's image&quot; is explicitly spelled out. It's the likely reason for the similarities one sees to Garou and Fera in this game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't fight to defend nature, because nature can defend itself just fine in Creation. </div> </div> </div>Technically, what the Garou and Fera are there to do is combat primordial corruption. In a modern context, it often involves prevention of environmental damage, but they were doing it long, long before any of those things were a problem. They tangled with Zmei, they imprisoned the Talons of the Wyrm when it tried to put a hand through (vaguely kind of; it could easily be more allegorical), and stopped an incursion of the Beast of War as well. Mokole had an even longer tenure prior to modern times, stretching back to when reptiles first appeared. And, like the Lunars, they did undergo quite a few changes (notably, though this is recent in how it was detailed, in how Mokole were once able to reproduce among one another and call in wondrous and impossible things into the world, until the Dragon Wars happened and they fucked up even worse than the Garou have).<br /> <br /> What this translates to in a &quot;squint and look sideways&quot; is conflict against an order gone wrong. Which is what their struggle with the Realm is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't champion or defend the dispossessed, but instead sacrifice them in droves to buy a few more years for themselves. </div> </div> </div>Not a few more years for themselves, a few less years for the Terrestrials and the Sidereals behind them. As you note below, they don't rely on reproduction to exist. They can keep weathering the Realm's First Age artifice down until it collapses and they finally free themselves of their entanglement to the state of the world, becoming something else yet again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't represent any tribal societies or lineages because they're Celestial Exalted, set above and apart from the rest of their peoples, and the only marks of their heritage are beastfolk, born as living weapons for their forebears' sakes and basically as wronged by their progenitors as anyone they're sent to fight. </div> </div> </div>Lots of beastfolk are slated to have nothing to do with Lunars in this edition (thankfully). Holden mentioned a few days, maybe a week ago that one of the reasons could be that the Wyld sweeps through, among other, non-Lunar causes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even when they do represent, defend, or otherwise give patronage to mortal societies, the devs themselves are on record that it's never made sense to <i>want </i>a Lunar in charge of anything - say (caveat: the devs have not said this, and it is purely my inference based on their statements), if someone in Perfect Soul's position were to be chosen by Luna instead of Sol, they would be <i>wrong </i>to do what she did; to kick out the occupiers and reassert themselves as the legitimate authority. </div> </div> </div>It's not their greatest strength, but it doesn't mean you don't want one in charge at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Barring some major setting revelations to shake things up, 3e Lunars don't come across as Werewolf: the Apocalypse. They come across as Beast: the Primordial. <i>I have nothing nice to say about Beast.</i> </div> </div> </div>Read more W:tA? It has old legends of battle, a changing society (there used to not be tribes, after all), and a breed of changers that's slowly incorporating humans, maybe (Rokea). The parallels are far from absent, even if they don;t leap out at every reader quite so obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:31:00-07:00","id":898087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897611#post897611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting video where a Dev talks about how how the Exalt types are explicitly the predecessors to WoD splats. I think it's safe to say that some of what he is expressing there has sunk into irrelevance in Modern Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly with the splats literally becoming them. They definitely still resemble them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't accept this as fact. It's also a disingenuous argument because it assumes doing the same thing over and over again using different 'types' of 'shapeshifting. I assume that when designing Lunars you would have them do certain things, certain ways to preserve thematic. </div> </div> </div>2e had no such ways, incidentally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A) Did I mention I really mislike W:tA? Cause I really dislike it. </div> </div> </div>And I utterly hate Mage, but it gets me nowhere to say that in conversations about changing Sidereals (the Sidereals having had a much better mechanical execution without authors starting a rebellion and completely rejecting their assignment to write outside their directives). Likewise, Vampire and Abyssals. I also hate Demon, but Infernals were a bit far away from that. I'm not crying if they get rid of the Coadjutor, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> B) Ex1 Lunars is widely considered one of the worst books in the franchise, on the same level as Scroll of the Monk or the first two chapters of Infernals. Ex2 Lunars stepped away from that and, when it was released, was actually quite beloved. It's overtime it's flaws have become apparent. It really feels like continuing the course away from Ex1 Lunars is the better path rather than racing back to it. </div> </div> </div>EX1 suffered from freelancers who didn't want to write it and thought it sucked, and various questionable mechanical details. EX2 was tepid and a patchwork of everything else. Never has a Lunar book been written with energy and genuine enthusiasm for the underlying subject matter of shifting through a multitude of beasts; if 2e Lunars had lots of people admire it, it was because it was wearing something else's skin, and that's too meta to use in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Po-tay-toe, Po-tah-toe? You can say it isn't shapeshifting but you can enact such radical changes it's as much shapeshifting as many of the things you've already described as shapeshifting. </div> </div> </div>Axiomatically no, again<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I literially just repeated what you said back to you and you're disagreeing with me...? Whatever. As far as Abyssal not getting grotesque stuff? I'll beleive it when I see it, especially as the core says stuff like &quot;others embody the grave\u2019s decay, becoming drawn and withered, or even blooming into full and eternal rot.&quot; and &quot;ingenious war machines of bone and sinew.&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That was the stated plan - the Liminals get things like bones erupting out into armor, and Abyssals go in another direction entirely. Also, just because an Abyssal resembles a zombie or mummified corpse doesn't mean that their powers will enhance said grotesque status..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You keep putting words in my mouth, it's a bit obnoxious. I never said I really wanted them to cover every type of shapeshifter, just not starting from a basis of W;tA. I should not that even THAT doesn't confine itself to just 'werewolf' shapeshifting, as they do more than just, you know, turn into a wolf or wolfman. </div> </div> </div>We still have heart's blood shapeshifting and I was talking about changing into animals and other humans in a broad sense. What did you think I was arguing about on the first go around and why did you think I meant The Five Forms?<br /> <br /> (Heart's Blood being far easier to work with than waiting to get to Rank 4 or 5 for the appropriate Gifts. Then again, Mokole can get really huge a lot easier, so tradeoff.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:40:33-07:00","id":898103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898008#post898008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I mean that's what concerns me the most about <i>Third Edition's</i> direction for Lunars - throwing hundreds-to-thousands of expendable dupes into pointless meat-grinder conflicts for purely-selfish reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstand my problem. MoEP: Lunars used this building of mortal societies as a way to have a lot of elder Lunars that didn't seem to be doing very much so the question of &quot;What's Tamuz doing?&quot; was answered by non-descript things behind the scenes of Chiaroscuro.<br /> <br /> I don't think it even intended to create the skinwalker illuminati but that's really the TSR at its most usable. Otherwise the PCs learn Lunars are behind the existence of their favourite cities and the reaction's &quot;well... good for them&quot; and feel sorta guilty about planning to use Taboo Inflicting Diatribe to end Delzhan sexism. If Tamuz is someone who'll hit back there's a point to him being there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T16:49:43-07:00","id":898383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897818#post897818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call it more of a whitewash myself.<br /> Either Lunar influence is so effective that no mortal can resist it. The TSR is impossible.<br /> Or.<br /> There's mortals who can and do resist but then they're a loose end. The TSR is basically the worst aspects of Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of TSR is not creating a society sans Exalted. It's creating a society that can operate with or without them. Meaning, a society can have Exalted in it, but because of the way it's organized, it can continue to exist despite a sudden lack of Exalted.<br /> <br /> You know, so the whole thing doesn't come crumbling down in case one guy dies. Which of course, is insane, because why would you want a civilization that can outlive you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:05:02-07:00","id":898403,"title":"","content":"I think the First Age ending in collapse rather than just ending owes more to the Solars being gone as a result of extreme violence, rather than just gone.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's hard to have any kind of complex system that can remain functional without certain key elements; dependence on your heart for everything else to work is not a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> I think the setting depicted societies that were as functional as you can expect under those circumstances and resources without direct Exalted action since the First Edition core.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of some people trying to transition society to a less interdependent state is an interesting goal for some individuals (more than large movements), but is more morally compromised than many people who have expressed attachment to the Thousand Streams River would seem to like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T18:53:15-07:00","id":898480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898403#post898403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the First Age ending in collapse rather than just ending owes more to the Solars being gone as a result of extreme violence, rather than just gone.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's hard to have any kind of complex system that can remain functional without certain key elements; dependence on your heart for everything else to work is not a conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Realm's crippling dependence on the Empress for any of its state functions to work expressly a conspiracy? Also there are reasons we in the modern world have moved away from monarchic or oligarchic rule, and a big one is that it kinda sucks when your head of state dies and you get a brutal succession crisis instead of a smooth transition!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898403#post898403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the setting depicted societies that were as functional as you can expect under those circumstances and resources without direct Exalted action since the First Edition core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the big problem with the TSR was that it was completely-incongruous with the setting's own conceits, especially the one that humanity would always need the Exalted, and for more reasons than just protecting humanity from other Exalted. You shouldn't really give a PC splat a primary goal where failure is a foregone conclusion (at least, not in Exalted - maybe in the World of Darkness, where it'd add to the pathos). Which brings us to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898403#post898403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea of some people trying to transition society to a less interdependent state is an interesting goal for some individuals (more than large movements), but is more morally compromised than many people who have expressed attachment to the Thousand Streams River would seem to like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morally-compromised goals and shades of grey are great for compelling storytelling. The 3e Silver Pact...doesn't really come across as grey. They come across as even more selfish and nihilistic than 1e Abyssals. They're against the Realm - who isn't? - but they aren't <i>for </i>anything, except whatever vague future awaits after all of their chains to the past fall away, and I mean come on, that's the exact same narrative problem the <i>Neverborn </i>have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:29:11-07:00","id":898502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898480#post898480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morally-compromised goals and shades of grey are great for compelling storytelling. The 3e Silver Pact...doesn't really come across as grey. They come across as even more selfish and nihilistic than 1e Abyssals. They're against the Realm - who isn't? - but they aren't <i>for </i>anything, except whatever vague future awaits after all of their chains to the past fall away, and I mean come on, that's the exact same narrative problem the <i>Neverborn </i>have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Lunars are going to keep existing after that, for one. For another, they have idealists who prefer to avoid collateral damage (hello 1e Tamuz, it's been a while).<br /> <br /> Edit: It's kind like someone who experienced something so terrible, that they found it difficult to concentrate on anything else besides removing the source of their trauma. They can probably do other things, but the impact of the prior event screams at them to address it first, and finish things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-24-2016, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:36:54-07:00","id":898509,"title":"","content":"I think the Lunars are for the experience of life as a cool shapeshifting hero without having to worry about the external danger of the empire at the centre of the world sending people to kill you repeatedly and the internal pressures of having protective impulses and directionless fury concerning something that no longer exists.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think &quot;living for the pursuit of personal happiness without having to worry about squads being sent to kill me&quot; is a fairly reasonable position to hold, which does not require much of an addendum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:39:23-07:00","id":898513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly with the splats literally becoming them. They definitely still resemble them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than Lunars? Not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e had no such ways, incidentally.</div> </div> </div> </div>...? I litterially can't parse what you mean here... Ex2 has no ways of shapeshifting...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I utterly hate Mage, but it gets me nowhere to say that in conversations about changing Sidereals (the Sidereals having had a much better mechanical execution without authors starting a rebellion and completely rejecting their assignment to write outside their directives). Likewise, Vampire and Abyssals. I also hate Demon, but Infernals were a bit far away from that. I'm not crying if they get rid of the Coadjutor, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those resemble each other. I would honestly have never made the connection without people telling me as much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EX1 suffered from freelancers who didn't want to write it and thought it sucked, and various questionable mechanical details. EX2 was tepid and a patchwork of everything else. Never has a Lunar book been written with energy and genuine enthusiasm for the underlying subject matter of shifting through a multitude of beasts; if 2e Lunars had lots of people admire it, it was because it was wearing something else's skin, and that's too meta to use in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ex1 Luanrs was rotten from inception, conceived of as an antagonist splat, outlined as barbarian funtime adventures and written by people who wanted to inject realpolitiks into it.<br /> <br /> And no, sorry. You don't get to decide why people liked something. Ex2 Lunars, as bad as it was, was a breath of fresh air compared to Ex1 and was genuinely loved at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Axiomatically no, again<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://gifs.joelglovier.com/classics/you-keep-using-that-word.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I'm sorry you're just...wrong. To any casual observer it's shapeshifting. Sure maybe it's just a supernaturally advanced disguise, but when it can enact such physical change that is completely impenetrable to any mundane scrutiny you've reach the point where a sufficiently advanced disguise in indistinguishable from shapeshifting and thus they are effectively the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the stated plan - the Liminals get things like bones erupting out into armor, and Abyssals go in another direction entirely. Also, just because an Abyssal resembles a zombie or mummified corpse doesn't mean that their powers will enhance said grotesque status..</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it a bit amusing you were going on about the Vampire connection earlier but now are on about how Abyssals don't do grotesque... Anyways, they still get constructions made of flesh and bone, so I feel like this is the sort of thing a Abyssal might do still, regardless of what other thematic whatever you're on about. Seriously dude. Two splats can do similiar things and the gameline won't implode. The devs have been very open about their non-respect of niche protection,, so just cool you jets about 'ZOMG ANOTHER SPLAT DOES THAT SO THIS SPLAT CAN'T'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898087#post898087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We still have heart's blood shapeshifting and I was talking about changing into animals and other humans in a broad sense. What did you think I was arguing about on the first go around and why did you think I meant The Five Forms?<br /> <br /> (Heart's Blood being far easier to work with than waiting to get to Rank 4 or 5 for the appropriate Gifts. Then again, Mokole can get really huge a lot easier, so tradeoff.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm arguing that even your precious W;tA is an amalgamation of themes and is by no ways really 'pure' to a single source of inspiration and really feels of lesser value than the rest of the combined history of shapeshifters in media going back pretty much to the beginning of human culture.<br /> Lunars are the only splat that cling so tight to their original WoD inspiration. I can safely say I see pretty much nothing of Hunters in Ex3 Solar, I, personally think it's time Lunar let go as well. Again, I've ALREADY said that Ex3 Lunars will probably end up clinging closer to it's W;tA inspiration, in that I know the current plan is to try to do a more competently executed version of Ex1 Lunars. I just wish it would be otherwise cause I greatly dislike W:tA. I mean, oh well, I'll have fan rewrites and maybe Ex4 in 2060.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T00:40:18-07:00","id":898732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=897611#post897611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Po-tay-toe, Po-tah-toe? You can say it isn't shapeshifting but you can enact such radical changes it's as much shapeshifting as many of the things you've already described as shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The terminology matters, for a bunch of reasons. Thematically, it's important that Solar charms be presented as a supernatural extension of skill, which shapeshifting isn't a good fit for; &quot;I am so skilled that I can even disguise myself as a dragon, and nobody can tell the difference even if they try to touch me&quot; (which they can't even actually do with their published charms, but which might make sense somewhere in their charmset) is <i>very different</i>, thematically, from &quot;I bend and twist my body into the form of a dragon&quot;<br /> <br /> It also matters because it tells you where your charms go from there. &quot;With my peerless talent at disguise, I can disguise myself as the Scarlet Empress so well that nobody can see through it&quot; <i>might</i> go to &quot;With my peerless talent at disguise, I can even disguise myself as a <i>dragon!</i>&quot; It probably does not extend to &quot;I can turn into a dragon, then breathe fire at people as an effective combat trick.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whereas, say &quot;I can shapeshift into a perfect duplicate of the Scarlet Empress&quot; might go there.<br /> <br /> I mean, I also have severe doubts about the underlying mechanism here. If I had to nail down the exact supernatural methods used by Solar disguise charms any more specifically than &quot;peerless skill at disguise&quot;, I would probably say that they work through supernaturally-intense deception (sometimes automatically-successful deception), akin to illusions -- not through changing any aspect of your physical body. If my character is short and I use Solar magic to disguise myself as someone much taller than I am, it doesn't let me reach things on the top shelf; it just ensures that I'm so persuasive and clever that nobody will notice or think it odd that I don't seem to reach things on the top shelf. If I'm a huge guy and disguise myself as a tiny girl, I won't be able to slip through tiny crevices -- I'll just be very good at coming up with excuses why I can't.<br /> <br /> (Granted that in that last case in particular &quot;slipping through small areas&quot; probably fits into Larceny, so I might have other magic that would cover me. But I'm not actually tiny, I'm just convincing people I am, and there are serious implications to that even if it serves some of the same purposes as shapeshifting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:44:10-07:00","id":898907,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Exalted are the Chosen of the Dead, and so they can choose to look like pristinely beautiful vampires (just as some ghosts can assume pristinely beautiful forms) or they can choose to look like decayed corpses or animated skeletons, because those things say &quot;death and the dead&quot; to people. But all of their Charms will evoke ghosts. Not corpses, but ghosts.<br /> <br /> Liminals are Frankenstein. They don't get to LOOK like skeletons, because their bodies need to actually function to sustain their unnatural lives. But their bodies are the source of their power, so they manipulate the substance of those bodies. They twist the meat, sprout the bone, strangle with their breath, and drown you with their blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone can be a cyborg; it's not just limited to the Alchemical Exalted. Solars, Dragon-Blooded, Sidereals, and Abyssals can all replace lost (or perfectly good) limbs and organs with artifacts.<br /> <br /> But Alchemicals are the only splat who base their entire CHARMSET around prosthetic machines, so no one else will ever really look like or play like the Alchemical Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:25:26-07:00","id":899815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881101-can-lunars-shrink?p=898480#post898480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the Realm's crippling dependence on the Empress for any of its state functions to work expressly a conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually a response to possible conspiracies.<br /> See, the problem with running a system that can smoothly change the leadership from one person to another is, what stops someone from permanently taking you out of the equation? The Empress seized power and made her self absolutely essential to the Realm, so that her fellow DBs couldn't off her without causing a lot of problems.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately that means, without her Imperial Majesty the Realm is going straight to hell. Or at least an ugly succession war.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:52:20-07:00","id":899866,"title":"","content":"The setup of the Realm is a bit distinct from the case of the Usurpation, and even then I think the degree to which the whole &quot;the Empress is needed to run things&quot; part worked has been exaggerated.<br /> <br /> From the way it was described, and going by the example of many Imperial Chinese bureaucratic institutions, I think it was mostly a case of &quot;people were given titles that didn't really describe what their jobs were supposed to be, so when tasks were actually allocated they all needed to refer to the Empress to know who was supposed to be doing what&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T18:23:14-07:00","id":920682,"title":"","content":"<i>Strength</i><br /> <br /> <b>Devastating Ogre Enhancement</b> - for the rest of the scene, the Lunar swells to twice her mass, her bones thickening and her muscles doubling. Her Strength and Stamina are increased, but the bonuses count against her Excellency dice-adding limits.<br /> <br /> <b>Emperor Ox Expansion</b> - for the duration of one attack or feat of strength, the Lunar explodes in size, striking with far greater mass, lifting with superior leverage, or absorbing damage with thicker flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Mountainous Spirit Expression</b> - the Lunar may use Heart's Blood to reflexively shapeshift into a creature larger than a man, but not so large as to have the Legendary Size merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Towering Beast Form</b> - the Lunar may use the stolen Heart's Blood of a creature with the Legendary Size merit. Shapeshifting into such a form requires an action which cannot be flurried.<br /> <br /> <b>God-Beast Transcendence</b> - the Lunar may now flurry another action -- including an attack -- with an action to shapeshift into a creature with the Legendary Size merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Body-Breaking Kata</b> - the Lunar enjoys greater faculty when attacking or grappling an opponent smaller than herself<br /> <br /> <b>Angry Rhino Charge</b> - this Charm may supplement the first non-projectile attack the Lunar makes in the same turn that she entered close range with the target smaller than she is. The attack's damage is greatly enhanced. This can also be used to enhance a grappling gambit.<br /> <br /> <b>Flying Tiger Technique</b> - supplementing a Move action or a successful Disengage or Withdraw action, the Lunar leaps one whole range band in any direction, regardless of terrain, as long as there is a clear path. This Charm likewise allows a swimming or flying Lunar to force his way through one range band of water or air currents strong enough to qualify as difficult terrain, or for a swimming Lunar to leap from the waters into the sky. Finally, it allows a flying Lunar to trade altitude for forward movement at a superior rate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Dexterity</i><br /> <br /> <b>Humble Mouse Shape</b> - the Lunar may use the stolen Heart's Blood of a creature smaller than a house cat.<br /> <br /> <b>Emerald Grasshopper Form</b> - the Lunar may use Heart's Blood reflexively shapeshift into a creature smaller than a man, but not smaller than a house cat.<br /> <br /> <b>Butterfly Eyes Defense </b>- the Lunar avoids an attack by exploding into a swarm of smaller creatures, either reforming instantly after the danger has passed or remaining in that shape amidst a distracting cloud of duplicates; they quickly fade, but may offer an opportunity to escape from sight.<br /> <br /> <b>Butterfly Eyes Feint</b> - the Lunar circumvents a defense in a similar fashion to Butterfly Eyes Defense, allowing them to strike from unexpected angles. This may be used against a Clash attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Tyrant Mouse Dominion</b> - the Lunar enjoys greater faculty when attacking or evading an opponent larger than himself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-24-2016, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}